"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "D",
"solution": "The variable terms in the second equation are \\(-2\\) times those in the first, so elimination will test whether their constants are compatible. Multiplying the first equation by \\(2\\) gives\n\\[\n4x-6y=16.\n\\]\nAdding this to \\(6y-4x=9\\) yields\n\\[\n0=25.\n\\]\nAny common solution would have to satisfy this equality, which is impossible. Therefore there is no solution, choice D.",
