"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "A",
"solution": "After the \\(15\\) girls leave, the girls' count stays unchanged while the \\(45\\) boys leave. Use this unchanged count to compare the two ratios.\n\nAt the end, every group of \\(5\\) girls corresponds to \\(1\\) boy. Before the boys left, those same \\(5\\) girls corresponded to \\(2\\cdot5=10\\) boys. Thus each group accounts for \\(10-1=9\\) of the boys who left.\n\nThere must therefore be \\(45/9=5\\) such groups of girls. The number of girls remaining is \\(5\\cdot5=25\\), so the original number was\n\\[\n25+15=40.\n\\]\nThus there were \\(40\\) girls originally, choice \\(\\mathrm{A}\\).",
