"answer": "B",
"solution": "A matching formula must agree with every column. The column \\(x=4\\), \\(y=6\\) is useful because the five choices give different outputs there. Substituting \\(x=4\\) into choices A through E gives, respectively,\n\\[\n4,\\quad 6,\\quad 24,\\quad 0,\\quad 12.\n\\]\nThus only B can match the table.\n\nTo check all the entries, write B as\n\\[\ny=x^2-3x+2=(x-1)(x-2).\n\\]\nFor \\(x=2,3,4,5,6\\), this gives \\(y=0,2,6,12,20\\), exactly as displayed. The matching formula is \\(y=x^2-3x+2\\), choice B.",
