"batch": "NA",
"number": 23,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "If the margin made on an article costing \\(C\\) dollars and selling for \\(S\\) dollars is \\(M=\\dfrac1nC,\\) then the margin is given by:",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(M=\\dfrac1{n-1}S\\)",
"B": "\\(M=\\dfrac1nS\\)",
"C": "\\(M=\\dfrac n{n+1}S\\)",
"D": "\\(M=\\dfrac1{n+1}S\\)",
"E": "\\(M=\\dfrac n{n-1}S\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "D",
"solution": "Interpret the margin as the dollar profit \\(M=S-C\\), with positive cost and profit in the ordinary sales setting. The relation \\(M=C/n\\) therefore has \\(n>0\\). It gives\n\\[\nC=nM.\n\\]\nThe selling price consists of the cost plus the profit, so\n\\[\nS=C+M=nM+M=(n+1)M.\n\\]\nSince \\(n+1>0\\), dividing by it is valid. Hence\n\\[\n\\boxed{M=\\frac{S}{n+1}},\n\\]\nwhich is choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
"sourceURL": "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/amc12/1954/solutions",
