"question": "Which one of the following is not equivalent to \\(0.000000375?\\)",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(3.75\\times10^{-7}\\)",
"B": "\\(3\\dfrac34\\times10^{-7}\\)",
"C": "\\(375\\times10^{-9}\\)",
"D": "\\(\\dfrac38\\times10^{-7}\\)",
"E": "\\(\\dfrac{3}{8000000}\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "D",
"solution": "The given decimal can be written as\n\\[\n0.000000375=\\frac{375}{10^9}=3.75\\times10^{-7}.\n\\]\nThus choice \\(\\text{A}\\) is equivalent. Choice \\(\\text{B}\\) is also equivalent because \\(3\\frac34=3.75\\), and choice \\(\\text{C}\\) equals \\(375/10^9\\). For choice \\(\\text{E}\\), multiplying numerator and denominator by 125 gives\n\\[\n\\frac{3}{8000000}=\\frac{375}{1000000000},\n\\]\nagain the given number.\n\nBut choice \\(\\text{D}\\) equals\n\\[\n\\frac38\\times10^{-7}\n=0.375\\times10^{-7}\n=3.75\\times10^{-8},\n\\]\nwhich is one tenth of the given number. Therefore the non-equivalent expression is \\(\\boxed{\\frac38\\times10^{-7}}\\), choice \\(\\text{D}\\).",
