"question": "The smaller angle between the hands of a clock at \\(12{:}25\\) p.m. is:",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(132^\\circ30'\\)",
"B": "\\(137^\\circ30'\\)",
"C": "\\(150^\\circ\\)",
"D": "\\(137^\\circ32'\\)",
"E": "\\(137^\\circ\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "B",
"solution": "The hour hand moves gradually between the hour marks, so its movement during the 25 minutes must be included. The minute hand moves \\(360/60=6^\\circ\\) per minute, placing it \\(25\\cdot6=150^\\circ\\) clockwise from 12.\n\nThe hour hand moves \\(30^\\circ\\) in 60 minutes, so it is\n\\[\n25\\cdot\\frac{30}{60}=12.5^\\circ\n\\]\nclockwise from 12. The difference is \\(150^\\circ-12.5^\\circ=137.5^\\circ\\). Since this is less than \\(180^\\circ\\), it is the smaller angle.\n\nFinally, \\(0.5^\\circ=0.5\\cdot60'=30'\\), so the answer is \\(\\boxed{137^\\circ30'}\\), choice \\(\\text{B}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
