"batch": "NA",
"number": 13,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "The fraction \\(\\dfrac{a^{-4}-b^{-4}}{a^{-2}-b^{-2}}\\) is equal to:",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(a^{-6}-b^{-6}\\)",
"B": "\\(a^{-2}-b^{-2}\\)",
"C": "\\(a^{-2}+b^{-2}\\)",
"D": "\\(a^2+b^2\\)",
"E": "\\(a^2-b^2\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "C",
"solution": "The negative exponents require \\(a\\ne0\\) and \\(b\\ne0\\). The denominator must also be nonzero, so \\(a^{-2}\\ne b^{-2}\\), equivalently \\(a^2\\ne b^2\\).\n\nThe numerator is a difference of squares. Factoring it reveals the denominator as a common factor:\n\\[\na^{-4}-b^{-4}=(a^{-2}-b^{-2})(a^{-2}+b^{-2}).\n\\]\nBecause \\(a^{-2}-b^{-2}\\ne0\\), we may cancel that factor:\n\\[\n\\frac{a^{-4}-b^{-4}}{a^{-2}-b^{-2}}\n=\\frac{(a^{-2}-b^{-2})(a^{-2}+b^{-2})}{a^{-2}-b^{-2}}\n=a^{-2}+b^{-2}.\n\\]\nThe original exclusions remain in force. The answer is \\(a^{-2}+b^{-2}\\), choice C.",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
"sourceURL": "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/amc12/1955/solutions",
