"solution": "Use one tenth of the square's side as the common unit of length. Its side then measures \\(10\\), and its area is \\(10\\cdot10=100\\) square units.\n\nSince \\(10\\%=1/10\\), ten percent of the square's side is \\(1\\) unit. The rectangle therefore has length \\(11\\) and width \\(9\\), giving area\n\\[\n11\\cdot9=99\n\\]\nsquare units. Both areas use the same unit, so their ratio is \\(99:100\\), choice A.",
