"question": "In checking the petty cash a clerk counts \\(q\\) quarters, \\(d\\) dimes, \\(n\\) nickels, and \\(c\\) cents. Later he discovers that \\(x\\) of the nickels were counted as quarters and \\(x\\) of the dimes were counted as cents. To correct the total obtained the clerk must:",
