"solution": "Only the miscounted coins affect the correction. Each nickel counted as a quarter contributes \\(25-5=20\\) cents too much, so the \\(x\\) nickels make the total \\(20x\\) cents too high.\n\nEach dime counted as a cent contributes \\(10-1=9\\) cents too little, so the \\(x\\) dimes make the total \\(9x\\) cents too low. Together, the errors leave the recorded total\n\\[\n20x-9x=11x\n\\]\ncents too high. The clerk must therefore subtract \\(\\boxed{11x\\text{ cents}}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{C}}\\). This formula also gives zero correction when \\(x=0\\).",
