"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "B",
"solution": "The coefficients tell us the sum and product of the roots without requiring their individual values. Because the quadratic is monic and has roots \\(r\\) and \\(s\\), with a repeated root counted twice, its factored form gives\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^2-px+q&=(x-r)(x-s)\\\\\n&=x^2-(r+s)x+rs.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nComparing coefficients yields \\(r+s=p\\) and \\(rs=q\\).\n\nNow expand the square of the sum:\n\\[\n(r+s)^2=r^2+2rs+s^2.\n\\]\nSubtracting \\(2rs\\) therefore gives\n\\[\nr^2+s^2=(r+s)^2-2rs=\\boxed{p^2-2q}.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{\\text{B}}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
"sourceURL": "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/amc12/1955/solutions",
