"level": "AMC 12",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 2,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "Mr. Jones sold two pipes at \\(\\$1.20\\) each. Based on the cost his profit on one was \\(20\\%\\) and his loss on the other was \\(20\\%.\\) On the sale of the pipes, he:",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "broke even",
"B": "lost \\(4\\)¢",
"C": "gained \\(4\\)¢",
"D": "lost \\(10\\)¢",
"E": "gained \\(10\\)¢"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "D",
"solution": "Each percentage is based on that pipe’s cost, so we must find the two costs separately. With a \\(20\\%\\) profit, the selling price is \\(120\\%\\) of cost; with a \\(20\\%\\) loss, it is \\(80\\%\\) of cost. Thus the costs, in dollars, are\n\\[\n\\frac{1.20}{1.20}=1.00\n\\qquad\\text{and}\\qquad\n\\frac{1.20}{0.80}=1.50.\n\\]\nThe total cost was \\(1.00+1.50=2.50\\) dollars, while the total selling price was \\(2(1.20)=2.40\\) dollars. He therefore lost \\(2.50-2.40=0.10\\) dollars, or \\(\\boxed{10\\text{¢},\\text{ choice D}}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
