"number": 13,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "Given two positive integers \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) with \\(x\\lt y.\\) The percent that \\(x\\) is less than \\(y\\) is:",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(\\dfrac{100(y-x)}x\\)",
"B": "\\(\\dfrac{100(x-y)}x\\)",
"C": "\\(\\dfrac{100(y-x)}y\\)",
"D": "\\(100(y-x)\\)",
"E": "\\(100(x-y)\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "C",
"solution": "The phrase “\\(x\\) is less than \\(y\\)” uses \\(y\\) as the comparison base. The amount of the decrease is \\(y-x\\). Since \\(y>0\\), divide the decrease by \\(y\\) and multiply by \\(100\\) to obtain the requested percent:\n\\[\n\\frac{y-x}{y}\\cdot100=\\frac{100(y-x)}{y}.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\dfrac{100(y-x)}{y}\\), choice C.",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
