"number": 20,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "If \\((0.2)^x=2\\) and \\(\\log 2=0.3010,\\) then the value of \\(x\\) to the nearest tenth is:",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(-10.0\\)",
"B": "\\(-0.5\\)",
"C": "\\(-0.4\\)",
"D": "\\(-0.2\\)",
"E": "\\(10.0\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "C",
"solution": "Use common, base-10 logarithms. Because \\(0.2=2/10\\), the quotient rule gives\n\\[\n\\log(0.2)=\\log2-\\log10\n=0.3010-1=-0.6990.\n\\]\nBoth sides of \\((0.2)^x=2\\) are positive, so taking logarithms is valid. The power rule brings the unknown exponent down as a multiplier:\n\\[\nx\\log(0.2)=\\log2.\n\\]\nSince \\(\\log(0.2)=-0.6990\\ne0\\), division gives\n\\[\nx\\approx\\frac{0.3010}{-0.6990}\n\\approx-0.4306.\n\\]\nRounded to the nearest tenth, the value is \\(-0.4\\), choice C.",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
"sourceURL": "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/amc12/1956/solutions",
