"year": 1956,
"level": "AMC 12",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 32,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "George and Henry started a race from opposite ends of the pool. After a minute and a half, they passed each other in the center of the pool. If they lost no time in turning and maintained their respective speeds, how many minutes after starting did they pass each other the second time?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(3\\)",
"B": "\\(4\\dfrac12\\)",
"C": "\\(6\\)",
"D": "\\(7\\dfrac12\\)",
"E": "\\(9\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "B",
"solution": "Because they first meet at the center, each swimmer covers half the pool in \\(1\\tfrac12\\) minutes. They cover equal distances in equal times, so their maintained speeds are equal.\n\nAfter passing, they swim apart. Each takes another \\(1\\tfrac12\\) minutes to reach the opposite end, arriving at three minutes after the start. They turn immediately and swim toward each other, meeting at the center after another \\(1\\tfrac12\\) minutes. There is no intervening meeting while they are swimming apart.\n\nThe second meeting occurs at\n\\[\n3+1\\tfrac12=\\boxed{4\\tfrac12\\text{ minutes}},\n\\]\nchoice B.",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
