"year": 1957,
"level": "AMC 12",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 16,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "Goldfish are sold at \\(15\\) cents each. The rectangular coordinate graph showing the cost of \\(1\\) to \\(12\\) goldfish is:",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "a straight line segment",
"B": "a set of horizontal parallel line segments",
"C": "a set of vertical parallel line segments",
"D": "a finite set of distinct points",
"E": "a straight line"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "D",
"solution": "Let \\(n\\) be the number of goldfish purchased, and measure cost in cents. Since goldfish are counted individually, the allowed inputs are exactly \\(n=1,2,\\ldots,12\\). The cost is \\(15n\\), so the graph consists of\n\\[\n(1,15),(2,30),\\ldots,(12,180).\n\\]\nThese twelve points are distinct because their first coordinates differ. Although they lie on one straight line, points between them would represent fractional numbers of goldfish and are not included. The graph is a finite set of distinct points, choice D.",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
"sourceURL": "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/amc12/1957/solutions",
"figureSources": {},
"editorialNote": "",
