"number": 34,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "The points that satisfy the system \\(x+y=1,\\) \\(x^2+y^2<25,\\) where the symbol “\\(<\\)” means “less than,” constitute the following set:",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "only two points",
"B": "an arc of a circle",
"C": "a straight line segment not including the\nend-points",
"D": "a straight line segment including the end-points",
"E": "a single point"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "C",
"solution": "Method 1: Interpret the line and circle\n\nThe equation \\(x+y=1\\), or \\(y=1-x\\), describes a straight line. The inequality \\(x^2+y^2<25\\) describes points strictly inside the circle centered at the origin with radius \\(5\\).\n\nThe point \\((0,1)\\) lies on the line and inside the circle, since \\(0^2+1^2=1<25\\). A line passing through an interior point of a circle crosses its circumference at two distinct points. The points of the line inside the circle form the segment between those crossings. The crossings themselves have \\(x^2+y^2=25\\), so the strict inequality excludes them. Thus the solution is a straight line segment without its endpoints, choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{C}}\\).\n\nMethod 2: Substitute and factor\n\nUse \\(x+y=1\\) to write \\(y=1-x\\). This makes the inequality a condition on just one coordinate:\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^2+(1-x)^2&<25,\\\\\n2x^2-2x-24&<0,\\\\\n(x-4)(x+3)&<0.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nThe product is negative exactly when the factors have opposite signs. This requires \\(x-4<0\\) and \\(x+3>0\\), giving \\(-3<x<4\\); the other opposite-sign possibility would require both \\(x>4\\) and \\(x<-3\\), which is impossible.\n\nEvery such \\(x\\) gives exactly one point \\((x,1-x)\\). As \\(x\\) ranges between \\(-3\\) and \\(4\\), these points fill the straight line segment between \\((-3,4)\\) and \\((4,-3)\\). At either endpoint, \\(x^2+y^2=25\\), so both endpoints are excluded. The answer is choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{C}}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
"sourceURL": "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/amc12/1957/solutions",
