"year": 1958,
"level": "AMC 12",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 3,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "Of the following expressions, the one equal to \\(\\dfrac{a^{-1}b^{-1}}{a^{-3}-b^{-3}}\\) is:",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(\\dfrac{a^2b^2}{b^2-a^2}\\)",
"B": "\\(\\dfrac{a^2b^2}{b^3-a^3}\\)",
"C": "\\(\\dfrac{ab}{b^3-a^3}\\)",
"D": "\\(\\dfrac{a^3-b^3}{ab}\\)",
"E": "\\(\\dfrac{a^2b^2}{a-b}\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "B",
"solution": "Negative powers mean reciprocals: \\(a^{-n}=1/a^n\\) for \\(a\\ne0\\). The original expression requires \\(a\\ne0\\), \\(b\\ne0\\), and \\(a^{-3}-b^{-3}\\ne0\\). First combine the denominator:\n\\[\na^{-3}-b^{-3}\n=\\frac1{a^3}-\\frac1{b^3}\n=\\frac{b^3-a^3}{a^3b^3}.\n\\]\nThus \\(b^3-a^3\\ne0\\). Dividing by this fraction means multiplying by its reciprocal, so\n\\[\n\\frac{a^{-1}b^{-1}}{a^{-3}-b^{-3}}\n=\\frac1{ab}\\cdot\\frac{a^3b^3}{b^3-a^3}\n=\\frac{a^2b^2}{b^3-a^3}.\n\\]\nThis equality retains the original restrictions on \\(a\\) and \\(b\\). The answer is choice B.",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
