"level": "AMC 12",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 26,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "A set of \\(n\\) numbers has the sum \\(s.\\) Each number of the set is increased by \\(20,\\) then multiplied by \\(5,\\) and then decreased by \\(20.\\) The sum of the numbers in the new set thus obtained is:",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(s+20n\\)",
"B": "\\(5s+80n\\)",
"C": "\\(s\\)",
"D": "\\(5s\\)",
"E": "\\(5s+4n\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "B",
"solution": "We can track the total without knowing the individual numbers. Adding \\(20\\) to each of the \\(n\\) numbers adds \\(20n\\) to their sum, making it \\(s+20n\\).\n\nMultiplying every number by \\(5\\) multiplies their sum by \\(5\\), by the distributive law. Finally, subtracting \\(20\\) from each number subtracts \\(20n\\) from the total. The resulting sum is\n\\[\n5(s+20n)-20n\n=5s+100n-20n\n=5s+80n.\n\\]\nThus the answer is \\(5s+80n\\), choice B.",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
"sourceURL": "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/amc12/1958/solutions",
