"year": 1959,
"level": "AMC 12",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 16,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "The expression \\[ \\frac{x^2-3x+2}{x^2-5x+6}\\div \\frac{x^2-5x+4}{x^2-7x+12}, \\] when simplified, is:",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(\\dfrac{(x-1)(x-6)}{(x-3)(x-4)}\\)",
"B": "\\(\\dfrac{x+3}{x-3}\\)",
"C": "\\(\\dfrac{x+1}{x-1}\\)",
"D": "\\(1\\)",
"E": "\\(2\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "D",
"solution": "Factoring exposes the common factors that can cancel. The identity\n\\[\n(x-r)(x-s)=x^2-(r+s)x+rs\n\\]\nlets us factor each quadratic by matching the sum and product of \\(r\\) and \\(s\\). The expression becomes\n\\[\n\\frac{(x-1)(x-2)}{(x-2)(x-3)}\n\\div\n\\frac{(x-1)(x-4)}{(x-3)(x-4)}.\n\\]\nThe original denominators require \\(x\\ne2,3,4\\). The fraction used as the divisor must also be nonzero, which additionally requires \\(x\\ne1\\).\n\nFor \\(x\\notin\\{1,2,3,4\\}\\), division by the second fraction is multiplication by its reciprocal:\n\\[\n\\frac{(x-1)(x-2)}{(x-2)(x-3)}\n\\cdot\n\\frac{(x-3)(x-4)}{(x-1)(x-4)}=1.\n\\]\nAll cancelled factors are nonzero on this domain. Thus the simplified value is \\(\\boxed{1}\\), choice \\(\\text{D}\\), with the original exclusions retained.",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
"sourceURL": "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/amc12/1959/solutions",
