"level": "AMC 12",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 3,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "Applied to a bill for \\(\\$10{,}000\\) the difference between a discount of \\(40\\%\\) and two successive discounts of \\(36\\%\\) and \\(4\\%,\\) expressed in dollars, is:",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(0\\)",
"B": "\\(144\\)",
"C": "\\(256\\)",
"D": "\\(400\\)",
"E": "\\(416\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "B",
"solution": "A successive discount applies to the amount remaining after the previous discount. A single \\(40\\%\\) discount leaves \\(60\\%\\) of the original bill, so the amount payable is\n\\[\n10000(0.60)=6000\n\\]\ndollars.\n\nFor the successive discounts, the \\(36\\%\\) discount first leaves \\(10000(0.64)=6400\\) dollars. The \\(4\\%\\) discount then leaves \\(96\\%\\) of this reduced amount, giving \\(6400(0.96)=6144\\) dollars.\n\nBecause both plans start with the same bill, the difference between the discount amounts equals the difference between the final bills:\n\\[\n6144-6000=144.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{144}\\) dollars, choice B.",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
