"year": 1960,
"level": "AMC 12",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 16,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "In the numeration system with base \\(5,\\) counting is as follows: \\(1,\\) \\(2,\\) \\(3,\\) \\(4,\\) \\(10,\\) \\(11,\\) \\(12,\\) \\(13,\\) \\(14,\\) \\(20,\\) \\(\\ldots\\) The number whose description in the decimal system is \\(69,\\) when described in the base \\(5\\) system, is a number with:",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "two consecutive digits",
"B": "two non-consecutive digits",
"C": "three consecutive digits",
"D": "three non-consecutive digits",
"E": "four digits"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "C",
"solution": "In base \\(5\\), each place is worth five times the place to its right, so the place values are \\(1,5,25,125,\\ldots\\). Since \\(25\\le69<125\\), the representation has three digits.\n\nThere are two groups of \\(25\\), leaving \\(19\\). Those \\(19\\) contain three groups of \\(5\\) and four ones. Therefore\n\\[\n69=2\\cdot25+3\\cdot5+4=234_5.\n\\]\nEach digit is allowed in base \\(5\\), and \\(2,3,4\\) are three consecutive digits. The answer is \\(\\boxed{\\text{C}}\\).",
