"level": "AMC 12",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 7,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "When simplified, the third term in the expansion of \\[ \\left(\\frac{a}{\\sqrt{x}}-\\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{a^2}\\right)^6 \\] is:",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(\\dfrac{15}{x}\\)",
"B": "\\(-\\dfrac{15}{x}\\)",
"C": "\\(-\\dfrac{6x^2}{a^9}\\)",
"D": "\\(\\dfrac{20}{a^3}\\)",
"E": "\\(-\\dfrac{20}{a^3}\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "A",
"solution": "For real values, the original expression requires \\(x>0\\) and \\(a\\ne0\\). In the usual binomial order, the first term uses six copies of the first summand, the second uses five copies and one second summand, and the third uses four copies and two second summands.\n\nThere are \\(6\\cdot5/2=15\\) ways to choose the two positions for the second summand: choosing the positions in order counts every pair twice. Thus the third term, denoted by \\(T_3\\), is\n\\[\nT_3=15\\left(\\frac{a}{\\sqrt{x}}\\right)^4\n\\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{a^2}\\right)^2.\n\\]\nThe two negative factors give a positive sign. Using \\((\\sqrt{x})^2=x\\), we obtain\n\\[\nT_3=15\\frac{a^4}{x^2}\\frac{x}{a^4}\n=\\frac{15}{x}.\n\\]\nThe cancellations are valid because \\(a\\ne0\\) and \\(x>0\\). The answer is \\(\\mathrm{A}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
"sourceURL": "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/amc12/1961/solutions",
