"number": 28,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "Five points \\(O,\\) \\(A,\\) \\(B,\\) \\(C,\\) \\(D\\) are taken in order on a straight line with distances \\(OA=a,\\) \\(OB=b,\\) \\(OC=c,\\) and \\(OD=d.\\) \\(P\\) is a point on the line between \\(B\\) and \\(C\\) and such that \\(AP:PD=BP:PC.\\) Then \\(OP\\) equals:",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(\\dfrac{b^2-bc}{a-b+c-d}\\)",
"B": "\\(\\dfrac{ac-bd}{a-b+c-d}\\)",
"C": "\\(-\\dfrac{bd+ac}{a-b+c-d}\\)",
"D": "\\(\\dfrac{bc+ad}{a+b+c+d}\\)",
"E": "\\(\\dfrac{ac-bd}{a+b+c+d}\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "B",
"solution": "Method 1: Write the segment lengths\n\nThe order of the points gives \\(0<a<b<c<d\\). Let \\(x=OP\\). Since \\(P\\) is between \\(B\\) and \\(C\\), we have \\(b<x<c\\), and the four relevant lengths are\n\\[\nAP=x-a,\\quad PD=d-x,\\quad BP=x-b,\\quad PC=c-x.\n\\]\nThus the given proportion is\n\\[\n\\frac{x-a}{d-x}=\\frac{x-b}{c-x}.\n\\]\nBoth denominators are positive, so cross-multiplication is valid:\n\\[\n(x-a)(c-x)=(x-b)(d-x).\n\\]\nExpanding reveals matching quadratic terms:\n\\[\n-x^2+(a+c)x-ac=-x^2+(b+d)x-bd.\n\\]\nAfter cancellation and collection,\n\\[\n(a-b+c-d)x=ac-bd.\n\\]\nThe coefficient of \\(x\\) is nonzero because\n\\[\na-b+c-d=-(b-a)-(d-c)<0.\n\\]\nTherefore \\(\\boxed{OP=\\dfrac{ac-bd}{a-b+c-d}}\\), choice B.\n\nMethod 2: Use the fixed outer segments\n\nThe differences \\(AP-BP=AB\\) and \\(PD-PC=CD\\) are fixed, which makes them useful for simplifying the proportion. Let its common ratio be\n\\[\nk=\\frac{AP}{PD}=\\frac{BP}{PC}>0.\n\\]\nThen \\(AP=kPD\\) and \\(BP=kPC\\). Subtracting these equations gives\n\\[\nAB=k\\,CD.\n\\]\nConsequently,\n\\[\n\\frac{BP}{PC}=k=\\frac{AB}{CD}=\\frac{b-a}{d-c}.\n\\]\nSo the segment \\(BC\\), whose length is \\(c-b\\), is divided into the positive ratio parts \\(b-a\\) and \\(d-c\\). Put \\(L=(b-a)+(d-c)>0\\). Then\n\\[\nBP=(c-b)\\frac{b-a}{L}.\n\\]\nBoth ratio parts are positive, so this places \\(P\\) strictly between \\(B\\) and \\(C\\), as required. Finally,\n\\[\nOP=b+BP\n=\\frac{bL+(c-b)(b-a)}{L}\n=\\frac{bd-ac}{L}.\n\\]\nSince \\(L=-(a-b+c-d)\\), this is \\(\\boxed{\\dfrac{ac-bd}{a-b+c-d}}\\), choice B.",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
"sourceURL": "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/amc12/1966/solutions",
