"number": 18,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "Side \\(AB\\) of triangle \\(ABC\\) has length \\(8\\) inches. Line \\(DEF\\) is drawn parallel to \\(AB\\) so that \\(D\\) is on segment \\(AC,\\) and \\(E\\) is on segment \\(BC.\\) Line \\(AE\\) extended bisects angle \\(FEC.\\) If \\(DE\\) has length \\(5\\) inches, then the length of \\(CE,\\) in inches, is:",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(\\dfrac{51}{4}\\)",
"B": "\\(13\\)",
"C": "\\(\\dfrac{53}{4}\\)",
"D": "\\(\\dfrac{40}{3}\\)",
"E": "\\(\\dfrac{27}{2}\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "D",
"solution": "The parallel cut determines a ratio, while the angle bisector will determine an actual length. Since \\(DE\\parallel AB\\), corresponding segments satisfy\n\\[\n\\frac{CE}{CB}=\\frac{DE}{AB}=\\frac58.\n\\]\nBecause \\(CB=CE+BE\\), this gives \\(CE:BE=5:3\\).\n\nLet \\(X\\) be a point on \\(AE\\) beyond \\(E\\). The ray \\(EA\\) lies inside \\(\\angle DEB\\), so its opposite ray \\(EX\\) lies inside the vertically opposite angle. Thus the given bisector condition places \\(F\\) on the extension of \\(DE\\) beyond \\(E\\).\n\nThe rays \\(EF\\) and \\(AB\\) have the same direction, as do \\(EX\\) and \\(AE\\). Parallelism therefore gives \\(\\angle BAE=\\angle FEX\\). The bisector condition gives \\(\\angle FEX=\\angle XEC\\). Finally, reversing both rays shows \\(\\angle XEC=\\angle AEB\\). Consequently\n\\[\n\\angle BAE=\\angle AEB.\n\\]\nTriangle \\(ABE\\) has equal angles at \\(A\\) and \\(E\\), so their opposite sides are equal: \\(BE=AB=8\\). Using the ratio already found,\n\\[\nCE=\\frac53\\,BE=\\frac53\\cdot8=\\boxed{\\frac{40}{3}}\\text{ inches},\n\\]\nchoice D.",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
"sourceURL": "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/amc12/1968/solutions",
