"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "In this diagram, not drawn to scale, figures \\(\\mathrm{I}\\) and \\(\\mathrm{III}\\) are equilateral triangular regions with respective areas of \\(32\\sqrt3\\) and \\(8\\sqrt3\\) square inches. Figure \\(\\mathrm{II}\\) is a square region with area \\(32\\) square inches. Let the length of segment \\(AD\\) be decreased by \\(12\\dfrac12\\%\\) of itself, while the lengths of \\(AB\\) and \\(CD\\) remain unchanged. The percent decrease in the area of the square is:\n\n[Figure 1](figures/1968_AMC_12_Q31_question_fig1.svg)",
