"year": 1969,
"level": "AMC 12",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 8,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "Triangle \\(ABC\\) is inscribed in a circle. The measures of the non-overlapping minor arcs \\(AB,\\) \\(BC,\\) and \\(CA\\) are, respectively, \\(x+75^\\circ,\\) \\(2x+25^\\circ,\\) \\(3x-22^\\circ.\\) Then one interior angle of the triangle, in degrees, is:",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(57\\dfrac12\\)",
"B": "\\(59\\)",
"C": "\\(60\\)",
"D": "\\(61\\)",
"E": "\\(122\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "D",
"solution": "The three non-overlapping arcs go around the circle once, so their measures sum to \\(360^\\circ\\):\n\\[\n(x+75^\\circ)+(2x+25^\\circ)+(3x-22^\\circ)=360^\\circ.\n\\]\nCombining terms gives \\(6x+78^\\circ=360^\\circ\\), hence \\(x=47^\\circ\\). The arc measures are therefore\n\\[\n\\widehat{AB}=122^\\circ,\\qquad\n\\widehat{BC}=119^\\circ,\\qquad\n\\widehat{CA}=119^\\circ.\n\\]\nEach is positive and less than \\(180^\\circ\\), as required for the stated minor arcs. The inscribed angle \\(\\angle ACB\\) intercepts arc \\(AB\\), so the inscribed angle theorem gives\n\\[\n\\angle ACB=\\frac12(122^\\circ)=61^\\circ.\n\\]\nThus one interior angle is \\(61^\\circ\\), choice D.",
