"year": 1970,
"level": "AMC 12",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 9,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "Points \\(P\\) and \\(Q\\) are on line segment \\(AB,\\) and both points are on the same side of the midpoint of \\(AB.\\) Point \\(P\\) divides \\(AB\\) in the ratio \\(2:3,\\) and \\(Q\\) divides \\(AB\\) in the ratio \\(3:4.\\) If \\(PQ=2,\\) then the length of segment \\(AB\\) is:",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(12\\)",
"B": "\\(28\\)",
"C": "\\(70\\)",
"D": "\\(75\\)",
"E": "\\(105\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "C",
"solution": "Because \\(P\\) and \\(Q\\) are on the same side of the midpoint, they have the same nearer endpoint. Call that endpoint \\(E\\), and let \\(L=AB\\).\n\nThe ratio \\(2:3\\) divides the whole segment into \\(2+3=5\\) equal parts, so \\(EP=2L/5\\). Similarly, \\(EQ=3L/7\\). Subtracting these distances from the same endpoint gives\n\\[\nPQ=\\left(\\frac37-\\frac25\\right)L\n=\\frac{15-14}{35}L\n=\\frac{L}{35}.\n\\]\nThus \\(L/35=2\\), giving \\(AB=70\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{C}}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
