"answer": "E",
"solution": "The hair-color categories divide all \\(50\\) girls into two separate groups. Since \\(31\\) are brunettes, the number of blondes is\n\\[50-31=19.\\]\nOf these blondes, \\(14\\) are blue-eyed, so \\(19-14=5\\) are brown-eyed.\n\nEvery brown-eyed girl is either blonde or brunette, and belongs to exactly one of those groups. Therefore the number of brown-eyed brunettes is\n\\[18-5=\\boxed{13},\\]\nchoice \\(\\boxed{\\text{E}}\\).",
