"level": "AMC 12",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 16,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "After finding the average of \\(35\\) scores, a student carelessly included the average with the \\(35\\) scores and found the average of these \\(36\\) numbers. The ratio of the second average to the true average was:",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(1:1\\)",
"B": "\\(35:36\\)",
"C": "\\(36:35\\)",
"D": "\\(2:1\\)",
"E": "None of these"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "A",
"solution": "Let \\(M\\) be the true average. Since the average equals the total divided by the number of scores, the original total is \\(35M\\). Adding the average therefore gives the new average\n\\[\n\\frac{35M+M}{36}=\\frac{36M}{36}=M.\n\\]\nThus the two averages are equal.\n\nIf \\(M\\ne0\\), their ratio is \\(M:M=1:1\\), giving choice A. If \\(M=0\\), as happens when all 35 scores are zero, both averages are zero and their numerical ratio is undefined. Therefore choice A requires the qualification that the true average is nonzero.",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
"sourceURL": "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/amc12/1971/solutions",
