"level": "AMC 12",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 4,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "The number of solutions to \\(\\{1,2\\}\\subseteq X\\subseteq\\{1,2,3,4,5\\},\\) where \\(X\\) is a subset of \\(\\{1,2,3,4,5\\},\\) is:",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(2\\)",
"B": "\\(4\\)",
"C": "\\(6\\)",
"D": "\\(8\\)",
"E": "None of these"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "D",
"solution": "The first inclusion requires \\(1\\) and \\(2\\) to belong to \\(X\\), and the second allows no elements outside \\(\\{1,2,3,4,5\\}\\). Thus only membership of \\(3\\), \\(4\\), and \\(5\\) remains undecided.\n\nEach of those three elements has two choices: include it or omit it. The multiplication principle gives\n\\[\n2\\cdot2\\cdot2=8.\n\\]\nEvery valid set makes exactly one such sequence of decisions, and different decisions produce different sets, so nothing is omitted or counted twice. Because the inclusions allow equality, both \\(\\{1,2\\}\\) and \\(\\{1,2,3,4,5\\}\\) are included. The answer is \\(8\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
