"level": "AMC 12",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 2,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "One thousand unit cubes are fastened together to form a large cube with edge length \\(10\\) units; this is painted and then separated into the original cubes. The number of these unit cubes which have at least one face painted is",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(600\\)",
"B": "\\(520\\)",
"C": "\\(488\\)",
"D": "\\(480\\)",
"E": "\\(400\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "C",
"solution": "It is easier to count the cubes with no paint. These are precisely the cubes inside the large cube, away from all six outer faces.\n\nAlong each of the three directions, exclude the first and last layers. That leaves \\(10-2=8\\) positions in each direction, so the unpainted interior contains\n\\[\n8\\cdot8\\cdot8=512\n\\]\nunit cubes. Every original cube is either unpainted or has at least one painted face. Thus the requested number is\n\\[\n1000-512=\\boxed{488},\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\text{C}\\). Subtracting the interior counts each remaining cube once, including those at edges and corners.",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
"sourceURL": "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/amc12/1973/solutions",
