"year": 1978,
"level": "AMC 12",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 5,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "Four boys bought a boat for \\(\\$60.\\) The first boy paid one half of the sum of the amounts paid by the other boys; the second boy paid one third of the sum of the amounts paid by the other boys; and the third boy paid one fourth of the sum of the amounts paid by the other boys. How much did the fourth boy pay?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(\\$10\\)",
"B": "\\(\\$12\\)",
"C": "\\(\\$13\\)",
"D": "\\(\\$14\\)",
"E": "\\(\\$15\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "C",
"solution": "For each boy, his payment together with the other boys' combined payment makes the full \\(\\$60\\). The first boy pays half as much as the others together, so these two amounts have ratio \\(1:2\\). His payment is therefore one of three equal parts of \\(60\\), or \\(60/3=20\\) dollars.\n\nThe second boy's payment and the rest have ratio \\(1:3\\), so he pays \\(60/4=15\\) dollars. The third boy's corresponding ratio is \\(1:4\\), so he pays \\(60/5=12\\) dollars. The fourth boy pays the remainder:\n\\[\n60-(20+15+12)=13.\n\\]\nThus the fourth boy paid \\(\\$13\\), choice C.",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
