"year": 1979,
"level": "AMC 12",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 19,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "Find the sum of the squares of all real numbers satisfying the equation \\(x^{256}-256^{32}=0.\\)",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(8\\)",
"B": "\\(128\\)",
"C": "\\(512\\)",
"D": "\\(65{,}536\\)",
"E": "\\(2(256^{32})\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "A",
"solution": "Writing the constant as a power of 2 makes its exponent match the exponent on \\(x\\):\n\\[\n256^{32}=(2^8)^{32}=2^{256}.\n\\]\nThus the equation is \\(x^{256}=2^{256}\\). Since 256 is even, \\(x^{256}=|x|^{256}\\). If \\(|x|<2\\), its 256th power is smaller than \\(2^{256}\\); if \\(|x|>2\\), its 256th power is larger. Consequently \\(|x|=2\\), giving exactly the two real solutions \\(x=2\\) and \\(x=-2\\). Both satisfy the original equation.\n\nThe requested sum is therefore\n\\[\n2^2+(-2)^2=4+4=\\boxed{8},\n\\]\nchoice A.",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
"sourceURL": "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/amc12/1979/solutions",
