"level": "AMC 8",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 20,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "In a certain year, January had exactly four Tuesdays and four Saturdays. On what day did January \\(1\\) fall that year?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "Monday",
"B": "Tuesday",
"C": "Wednesday",
"D": "Friday",
"E": "Saturday"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "C",
"solution": "January has \\(31=4\\cdot7+3\\) days. Its first \\(28\\) days form four complete weeks, giving four of every weekday. The remaining three dates, January \\(29\\), \\(30\\), and \\(31\\), have the same weekdays as January \\(1\\), \\(2\\), and \\(3\\). Those three weekdays therefore occur five times.\n\nSince Tuesday and Saturday occur exactly four times, neither can be among the first three weekdays of January. Around the week, the weekdays avoiding Tuesday and Saturday form two uninterrupted groups: Wednesday, Thursday, Friday; and Sunday, Monday. Only the first group contains three consecutive weekdays.\n\nThus January \\(1\\) was \\(\\boxed{\\text{Wednesday}}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{C}}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
"sourceURL": "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/amc8/1985/solutions",
