"number": 23,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "King Middle School has \\(1200\\) students. Each student takes \\(5\\) classes a day. Each teacher teaches \\(4\\) classes. Each class has \\(30\\) students and \\(1\\) teacher. How many teachers are there at King Middle School?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(30\\)",
"B": "\\(32\\)",
"C": "\\(40\\)",
"D": "\\(45\\)",
"E": "\\(50\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "E",
"solution": "Count each student's attendance at each daily class separately. Each of the \\(1200\\) students attends \\(5\\) classes, so the daily total is\n\\[\n1200\\cdot 5=6000\n\\]\nclass attendances.\n\nEach teacher teaches \\(4\\) classes with \\(30\\) students apiece, accounting for \\(4\\cdot 30=120\\) attendances. Since every class has exactly one teacher, every attendance belongs to exactly one teacher's total. Therefore the number of teachers is\n\\[\n\\frac{6000}{120}=50.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{50}\\) teachers, choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{E}}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
