"batch": "NA",
"number": 20,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "The value of the expression\n\n\\[\\frac{(304)^5}{(29.7)(399)^4}\\]\n\nis closest to",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(0.003\\)",
"B": "\\(0.03\\)",
"C": "\\(0.3\\)",
"D": "\\(3\\)",
"E": "\\(30\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "D",
"solution": "The choices are widely separated, so bounds can identify the closest value without calculating the large powers exactly. Let\n\\[\nE=\\frac{304^5}{29.7\\cdot399^4}.\n\\]\nAll the numbers are positive. Decreasing the numerator and increasing the denominator makes the fraction smaller, so\n\\[\nE>\\frac{300^5}{30\\cdot400^4}\n=10\\left(\\frac34\\right)^4\n=\\frac{810}{256}>3.\n\\]\nFor an upper bound, notice that \\(304<399\\) and \\(304<11\\cdot29.7=326.7\\). Therefore\n\\[\nE=\\frac{304}{29.7}\\left(\\frac{304}{399}\\right)^4<11.\n\\]\nThus \\(3<E<11\\). Every listed value below \\(3\\) is farther from \\(E\\) than \\(3\\) is. Also, \\(E\\) is less than \\(8\\) away from \\(3\\), but more than \\(19\\) away from \\(30\\). The closest listed value is \\(3\\), choice D.",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
"sourceURL": "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/amc8/1986/solutions",
