"number": 19,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "A calculator has a squaring key \\(\\boxed{x^2}\\) that replaces the number currently displayed with its square. For example, if the display reads \\(\\boxed{\\phantom{00}3}\\) and \\(\\boxed{x^2}\\) is pressed, the display becomes \\(\\boxed{\\phantom{00}9}.\\) If the display reads \\(\\boxed{\\phantom{00}2},\\) how many times must \\(\\boxed{x^2}\\) be pressed to produce a displayed number greater than \\(500?\\)",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(4\\)",
"B": "\\(5\\)",
"C": "\\(8\\)",
"D": "\\(9\\)",
"E": "\\(250\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "A",
"solution": "Each press squares the current display, so calculate the displays in order:\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{Press 1:}\\quad&2^2=4,\\\\\n\\text{Press 2:}\\quad&4^2=16,\\\\\n\\text{Press 3:}\\quad&16^2=256,\\\\\n\\text{Press 4:}\\quad&256^2=65\\,536.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nThe starting display and the displays after the first three presses are all below \\(500\\). The fourth press produces a number greater than \\(500\\), so the required number is \\(4\\) presses, choice A.",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
"sourceURL": "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/amc8/1987/solutions",
