"year": 1987,
"level": "AMC 8",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 23,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "Assume the adjoining chart shows the \\(1980\\) U.S. population, in millions, for each region by ethnic group. To the nearest percent, what percent of the U.S. Black population lived in the South?\n\n\\[\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|}\\hline & \\text{NE} & \\text{MW} & \\text{South} & \\text{West}\\\\ \\hline \\text{White} & 42 & 52 & 57 & 35\\\\ \\hline \\text{Black} & 5 & 5 & 15 & 2\\\\ \\hline \\text{Asian} & 1 & 1 & 1 & 3\\\\ \\hline \\text{Other} & 1 & 1 & 2 & 4\\\\ \\hline\\end{array}\\]",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(20\\%\\)",
"B": "\\(25\\%\\)",
"C": "\\(40\\%\\)",
"D": "\\(56\\%\\)",
"E": "\\(80\\%\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "D",
"solution": "The requested whole is the U.S. Black population, so add the four entries in the Black row:\n\\[\n5+5+15+2=27\\text{ million}.\n\\]\nOf these, \\(15\\) million lived in the South. Both counts are in millions, so their units cancel when forming the share:\n\\[\n\\frac{15}{27}\\times100\\%=55.555\\ldots\\%.\n\\]\nRounding to the nearest whole percent gives \\(56\\%\\), choice D.",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
