"level": "AMC 12",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 2,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "Triangles \\(ABC\\) and \\(XYZ\\) are similar, with \\(A\\) corresponding to \\(X\\) and \\(B\\) to \\(Y.\\) If \\(AB=3,\\) \\(BC=4,\\) and \\(XY=5,\\) then \\(YZ\\) is",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(3\\frac34\\)",
"B": "\\(6\\)",
"C": "\\(6\\frac14\\)",
"D": "\\(6\\frac23\\)",
"E": "\\(8\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "D",
"solution": "The stated correspondence also pairs \\(C\\) with \\(Z\\). Thus \\(AB\\) corresponds to \\(XY\\), and \\(BC\\) corresponds to \\(YZ\\).\n\nCorresponding sides of similar triangles have the same scale factor. From triangle \\(ABC\\) to triangle \\(XYZ\\), this factor is\n\\[\n\\frac{XY}{AB}=\\frac53.\n\\]\nApply it to the corresponding side \\(BC=4\\):\n\\[\nYZ=4\\cdot\\frac53=\\frac{20}{3}=6\\frac23.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{6\\frac23}\\), choice \\(\\text{D}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
