"number": 7,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "The expression \\(2.46 \\times 8.163 \\times (5.17 + 4.829)\\) is closest to",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(100\\)",
"B": "\\(200\\)",
"C": "\\(300\\)",
"D": "\\(400\\)",
"E": "\\(500\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "B",
"solution": "First add inside the parentheses: \\(5.17+4.829=9.999\\). Rounding the three factors to convenient nearby numbers suggests\n\\[\n2.46\\times8.163\\times9.999\n\\approx2.5\\times8\\times10=200.\n\\]\nWe can verify the closest choice without calculating the full product. Let \\(P\\) denote the exact product. We have\n\\[\n2.4<2.46<2.5,\\qquad 8<8.163<9,\n\\]\n\\[\n9<9.999<10.\n\\]\nAll factors are positive, so multiplying the lower bounds and the upper bounds gives\n\\[\n172.8=2.4\\times8\\times9<P<2.5\\times9\\times10=225.\n\\]\nThe midpoints between \\(200\\) and its neighboring choices \\(100\\) and \\(300\\) are \\(150\\) and \\(250\\). Since \\(150<P<250\\), the exact value is closest to \\(\\boxed{200}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{B}}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
