"solution": "The bushes surround the patio’s edge, so we need its circumference. With radius \\(12\\) feet, the distance around the patio is\n\\[\n2\\pi\\cdot12=24\\pi\\approx75.4\\text{ feet}.\n\\]\nGoing around a circle, each bush has one gap following it, including the gap from the last bush back to the first. Thus the number of bushes equals the number of gaps. With gaps of about \\(1\\) foot, approximately \\(\\boxed{75}\\) bushes are needed, choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\).",
