"batch": "NA",
"number": 17,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "The number \\(N\\) is between \\(9\\) and \\(17.\\) Which of the following could be the average of \\(6,\\) \\(10,\\) and \\(N?\\)",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(8\\)",
"B": "\\(10\\)",
"C": "\\(12\\)",
"D": "\\(14\\)",
"E": "\\(16\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "B",
"solution": "An average of three numbers is their total divided by \\(3\\). To test a proposed average, multiply it by \\(3\\) to recover the total, then subtract \\(6+10=16\\) to find the required value of \\(N\\). For the five choices, this gives\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{A: }&3\\times8-16=8,\\\\\n\\text{B: }&3\\times10-16=14,\\\\\n\\text{C: }&3\\times12-16=20,\\\\\n\\text{D: }&3\\times14-16=26,\\\\\n\\text{E: }&3\\times16-16=32.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nOnly \\(14\\) is between \\(9\\) and \\(17\\), and indeed \\((6+10+14)\\div3=10\\). Therefore the possible average is \\(10\\), choice B.",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
"sourceURL": "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/amc8/1989/solutions",
