"question": "An acute isosceles triangle, \\(ABC,\\) is inscribed in a circle. Through \\(B\\) and \\(C,\\) tangents to the circle are drawn, meeting at point \\(D.\\) If \\(\\angle ABC=\\angle ACB=2\\angle D\\) and \\(x\\) is the radian measure of \\(\\angle A,\\) then \\(x=\\)\n\n[Figure 1](figures/1990_AMC_12_Q14_question_fig1.svg)",
