"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "Which of the following is closest to the product \\((0.48017)(0.48017)(0.48017)?\\)",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(0.011 \\)",
"B": "\\(0.110 \\)",
"C": "\\(1.10 \\)",
"D": "\\(11.0 \\)",
"E": "\\(110 \\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "B",
"solution": "The choices are far apart, so bounds on the product are enough to determine the closest one. Let \\(P=(0.48017)(0.48017)(0.48017)\\). Since each positive factor is between \\(0.48\\) and \\(0.5\\),\n\\[\n0.48^3<P<0.5^3,\n\\]\nwhich gives\n\\[\n0.110592<P<0.125.\n\\]\nThus \\(P\\) is above \\(0.110\\) and less than \\(0.015\\) away from it. Its distance from \\(0.011\\) is greater than \\(0.110592-0.011=0.099592\\). Each remaining choice is at least \\(1.10\\), so its distance from \\(P\\) is greater than \\(1.10-0.125=0.975\\).\n\nTherefore the closest choice is \\(\\boxed{0.110}\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{B}\\).",
