"level": "AMC 8",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 9,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "The grading scale shown is used at Jones Junior High. The fifteen scores in Mr. Freeman’s class were: \\(89,\\) \\(72,\\) \\(54,\\) \\(97,\\) \\(77,\\) \\(92,\\) \\(85,\\) \\(74,\\) \\(75,\\) \\(63,\\) \\(84,\\) \\(78,\\) \\(71,\\) \\(80,\\) \\(90.\\)\n\n\\[\\begin{array}{|c|c|}\\hline \\text{A} & 93\\text{--}100\\\\ \\hline \\text{B} & 85\\text{--}92\\\\ \\hline \\text{C} & 75\\text{--}84\\\\ \\hline \\text{D} & 70\\text{--}74\\\\ \\hline \\text{F} & 0\\text{--}69\\\\ \\hline\\end{array}\\]\n\nIn Mr. Freeman’s class, what percent of the students received a grade of C?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(20\\% \\)",
"B": "\\(25\\% \\)",
"C": "\\(30\\% \\)",
"D": "\\(33\\dfrac{1}{3}\\% \\)",
"E": "\\(40\\% \\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "D",
"solution": "A grade of C includes scores from \\(75\\) through \\(84\\), including both endpoints. Checking the fifteen scores against that range gives exactly\n\\[\n75,\\ 77,\\ 78,\\ 80,\\ 84.\n\\]\nThese are five students. To find their percentage of the class, divide this count by the total number of students:\n\\[\n\\frac{5}{15}=\\frac13.\n\\]\nTherefore the percentage receiving C is\n\\[\n\\frac13\\cdot100\\%=33\\frac13\\%,\n\\]\nchoice D.",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
