"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "What is the value of the following expression?\n\n\\[ \\begin{aligned} &1990 - 1980 + 1970 - 1960 \\\\ &\\quad {}+ \\cdots - 20 + 10 \\end{aligned} \\]",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(-990 \\)",
"B": "\\(-10 \\)",
"C": "\\(990 \\)",
"D": "\\(1000 \\)",
"E": "\\(1990 \\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "D",
"solution": "Neighboring differences such as \\(1990-1980\\) and \\(1970-1960\\) each equal \\(10\\), so grouping these pairs simplifies the calculation:\n\\[\n(1990-1980)+(1970-1960)+\\cdots+(30-20)+10.\n\\]\nThere are \\(1990\\div10=199\\) terms, one for each multiple of \\(10\\) from \\(10\\) through \\(1990\\), with alternating signs. The first \\(198\\) terms form \\(99\\) separate pairs, leaving the final \\(+10\\) unpaired. Every term is included exactly once. Since each pair contributes \\(10\\), the expression equals\n\\[\n99\\cdot10+10=1000.\n\\]\nThe value is \\(1000\\), choice D.",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
