"batch": "NA",
"number": 20,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "The annual incomes of \\(1{,}000\\) families range from \\(\\$8200\\) to \\(\\$98{,}000.\\) In error, the largest income was entered on the computer as \\(\\$980{,}000.\\) The difference between the mean of the incorrect data and the mean of the actual data is",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(\\$882\\)",
"B": "\\(\\$980\\)",
"C": "\\(\\$1078\\)",
"D": "\\(\\$482{,}000\\)",
"E": "\\(\\$882{,}000\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "A",
"solution": "The mean equals the total income divided by the number of families. Since only one entry changed, the incorrect total exceeds the actual total by\n\\[\n980{,}000-98{,}000=882{,}000\n\\]\ndollars. Both means divide their totals by \\(1{,}000\\), so their difference is\n\\[\n\\frac{882{,}000}{1{,}000}=882\n\\]\ndollars. The answer is \\(\\$882\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{A}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
