"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "B",
"solution": "Count the multiples of each number, then correct for numbers counted in both groups. The multiples of \\(3\\) run from \\(3\\times1\\) through \\(3\\times15=45\\), giving \\(15\\) numbers; the next multiple, \\(48\\), exceeds \\(46\\). The multiples of \\(5\\) run from \\(5\\times1\\) through \\(5\\times9=45\\), giving \\(9\\) numbers; the next is \\(50\\).\n\nThe numbers appearing in both groups are \\(15,30,45\\). Adding the two counts includes each of these twice, so subtract their count once:\n\\[\n15+9-3=21.\n\\]\nEvery qualifying number belongs to at least one group, and after this correction each is counted once. The answer is \\(\\boxed{21}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{B}}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
