"year": 1991,
"level": "AMC 8",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 23,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "The Pythagoras High School band has \\(100\\) female and \\(80\\) male members. The Pythagoras High School orchestra has \\(80\\) female and \\(100\\) male members. There are \\(60\\) females who are members in both band and orchestra. Altogether, there are \\(230\\) students who are in either band or orchestra or both. The number of males in the band who are NOT in the orchestra is",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(10\\)",
"B": "\\(20\\)",
"C": "\\(30\\)",
"D": "\\(50\\)",
"E": "\\(70\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "A",
"solution": "The band has \\(100+80=180\\) members, and the orchestra has \\(80+100=180\\) members. Adding these totals counts every student once, except students in both groups, who are counted twice.\n\nThe excess over the \\(230\\) different students is therefore exactly the number in both groups:\n\\[\n180+180-230=130.\n\\]\nOf these, \\(60\\) are female, so \\(130-60=70\\) are male.\n\nThe band has \\(80\\) male members altogether. Removing the \\(70\\) who also belong to the orchestra leaves \\(80-70=\\boxed{10}\\) males in the band only, choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{A}}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
