"question": "Part of an “\\(n\\)-pointed regular star” is shown. It is a simple closed polygon in which all \\(2n\\) edges are congruent, angles \\(A_1,\\) \\(A_2,\\) \\(\\ldots,\\) \\(A_n\\) are congruent, and angles \\(B_1,\\) \\(B_2,\\) \\(\\ldots,\\) \\(B_n\\) are congruent. If the acute angle at \\(A_1\\) is \\(10^\\circ\\) less than the acute angle at \\(B_1,\\) then \\(n=\\)\n\n[Figure 1](figures/1992_AMC_12_Q20_question_fig1.svg)",
