"year": 1992,
"level": "AMC 8",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 18,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "On a trip, a car traveled \\(80\\) miles in an hour and a half, then was stopped in traffic for \\(30\\) minutes, then traveled \\(100\\) miles during the next \\(2\\) hours. What was the car’s average speed in miles per hour for the \\(4\\)-hour trip?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(45\\)",
"B": "\\(50\\)",
"C": "\\(60\\)",
"D": "\\(75\\)",
"E": "\\(90\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "A",
"solution": "Average speed is the total distance divided by the total elapsed time. The stop adds time to the trip but adds no distance, so it must be included in the four-hour total.\n\nThe car travels \\(80+100=180\\) miles altogether. Its average speed is therefore\n\\[\n\\frac{180\\text{ miles}}{4\\text{ hours}}=45\\text{ miles per hour}.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(45\\) miles per hour, choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{A}}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
"sourceURL": "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/amc8/1992/solutions",
"figureSources": {},
"editorialNote": "",
