"year": 1992,
"level": "AMC 8",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 22,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "Eight \\(1 \\times 1\\) square tiles are arranged as shown so their outside edges form a polygon with a perimeter of \\(14\\) units. Two additional tiles of the same size are added to the figure so that at least one side of each added tile is shared with a side of one of the squares in the original figure. Which of the following could be the perimeter of the new figure?\n\n[Figure 1](figures/1992_AMC_8_Q22_question_fig1.svg)",
"questionType": "mixed",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(15\\)",
"B": "\\(17\\)",
"C": "\\(18\\)",
"D": "\\(19\\)",
"E": "\\(20\\)"
},
