"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "If each of the three operation signs, \\(+,\\) \\(-,\\) \\(\\times,\\) is used exactly once in one of the blanks in the expression\n\n\\[5 \\, \\underline{\\phantom{x}} \\, 4 \\, \\underline{\\phantom{x}} \\, 6 \\, \\underline{\\phantom{x}} \\, 3\\]\n\nthen the value of the result could equal",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(9\\)",
"B": "\\(10\\)",
"C": "\\(15\\)",
"D": "\\(16\\)",
"E": "\\(19\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "E",
"solution": "We need a placement that produces one of the choices. Putting the multiplication sign between \\(6\\) and \\(3\\) gives a product of \\(18\\). We can use the remaining signs to add \\(5-4=1\\):\n\\[\n5-4+6\\times3=5-4+18=19.\n\\]\nThis uses each of \\(+\\), \\(-\\), and \\(\\times\\) exactly once. Therefore the result could equal \\(19\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{E}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
