"question": "\\(4^4\\cdot9^4\\cdot4^9\\cdot9^9=\\)",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(13^{13}\\)",
"B": "\\(13^{36}\\)",
"C": "\\(36^{13}\\)",
"D": "\\(36^{36}\\)",
"E": "\\(1296^{26}\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "C",
"solution": "Group the factors with the same base. Multiplying powers with the same base adds their exponents, so\n\\[\n4^4\\cdot9^4\\cdot4^9\\cdot9^9\n=4^{4+9}\\cdot9^{4+9}\n=4^{13}\\cdot9^{13}.\n\\]\nThe two remaining powers have the same exponent. Using \\(a^n b^n=(ab)^n\\), the product becomes\n\\[\n(4\\cdot9)^{13}=\\boxed{36^{13}},\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\text{C}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
