"year": 1995,
"level": "AMC 8",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 4,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "A teacher tells the class, “Think of a number, add \\(1\\) to it, and double the result. Give the answer to your partner. Partner, subtract \\(1\\) from the number you are given and double the result to get your answer.” Ben thinks of \\(6,\\) and gives his answer to Sue. What should Sue’s answer be?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(18\\)",
"B": "\\(24\\)",
"C": "\\(26\\)",
"D": "\\(27\\)",
"E": "\\(30\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "C",
"solution": "Ben adds \\(1\\) before doubling, so the number he gives Sue is\n\\[\n(6+1)\\cdot2=14.\n\\]\nSue starts with \\(14\\), subtracts \\(1\\), and then doubles:\n\\[\n(14-1)\\cdot2=\\boxed{26}.\n\\]\nSue's answer should be \\(26\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{C}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
"sourceURL": "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/amc8/1995/solutions",
