"year": 1995,
"level": "AMC 8",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 16,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "Students from three middle schools worked on a summer project. Seven students from Allen School worked for \\(3\\) days. Four students from Balboa School worked for \\(5\\) days. Five students from Carver School worked for \\(9\\) days. The total amount paid for the students’ work was \\(\\$774.\\) Assuming each student received the same amount for a day’s work, how much did the students from Balboa School earn altogether?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(\\$9.00\\)",
"B": "\\(\\$48.38\\)",
"C": "\\(\\$180.00\\)",
"D": "\\(\\$193.50\\)",
"E": "\\(\\$258.00\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "C",
"solution": "Count one student working for one day as one unit of work. Since every student receives the same daily pay, every such unit earns the same amount.\n\nAllen, Balboa, and Carver contributed \\(7\\times3=21\\), \\(4\\times5=20\\), and \\(5\\times9=45\\) units, respectively. Their earnings are therefore in the ratio \\(21:20:45\\). There are\n\\[\n21+20+45=86\n\\]\nequally paid units altogether, so each unit earns \\(774\\div86=9\\) dollars. Balboa's \\(20\\) units earn \\(20\\times9=180\\) dollars. Thus Balboa School's students earned \\(\\$180.00\\), choice C.",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
