"level": "AMC 8",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 17,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "The table below gives the percent of students in each grade at Annville and Cleona elementary schools:\n\n\\[\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|}\\hline & K & 1 & 2 & 3 & 4 & 5 & 6\\\\ \\hline \\text{Annville} & 16\\% & 15\\% & 15\\% & 14\\% & 13\\% & 16\\% & 11\\%\\\\ \\hline \\text{Cleona} & 12\\% & 15\\% & 14\\% & 13\\% & 15\\% & 14\\% & 17\\%\\\\ \\hline\\end{array}\\]\n\nAnnville has \\(100\\) students and Cleona has \\(200\\) students. In the two schools combined, what percent of the students are in grade \\(6?\\)",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(12\\%\\)",
"B": "\\(13\\%\\)",
"C": "\\(14\\%\\)",
"D": "\\(15\\%\\)",
"E": "\\(28\\%\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "D",
"solution": "The schools have different numbers of students, so first convert each school's percentage into a number of sixth graders. Annville has \\(11\\%\\cdot100=11\\) sixth graders, and Cleona has \\(17\\%\\cdot200=34\\).\n\nTogether, the schools have \\(11+34=45\\) sixth graders and \\(100+200=300\\) students. Thus the percentage in grade \\(6\\) is\n\\[\n\\frac{45}{300}\\cdot100\\%=15\\%.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{15\\%}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
