"number": 26,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "An urn contains marbles of four colors: red, white, blue, and green. When four marbles are drawn without replacement, the following events are equally likely:\n\n(a) the selection of four red marbles;\n\n(b) the selection of one white and three red marbles;\n\n(c) the selection of one white, one blue, and two red marbles; and\n\n(d) the selection of one marble of each color.\n\nWhat is the smallest number of marbles satisfying the given condition?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(19\\)",
"B": "\\(21\\)",
"C": "\\(46\\)",
"D": "\\(69\\)",
"E": "more than \\(69\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "B",
"solution": "Let \\(r,w,b,g\\) be the positive integer numbers of red, white, blue, and green marbles, and let \\(N=r+w+b+g\\). Every set of four individual marbles is equally likely, with the same probability denominator \\(\\binom N4\\). Thus equal event probabilities mean equal numbers of favorable sets.\n\nCounting by color, the four numbers are\n\\[\n\\binom r4,\\qquad\nw\\binom r3,\\qquad\nwb\\binom r2,\\qquad\nrwbg.\n\\]\nEach product chooses the required marbles within each color. Order is ignored, so each favorable set is counted once.\n\nSince all four colors are present, \\(rwbg>0\\). Equality therefore requires \\(r\\ge4\\). Equating consecutive counts and canceling positive factors gives\n\\[\n\\frac{r-3}{4}=w,\\qquad\n\\frac{r-2}{3}=b,\\qquad\n\\frac{r-1}{2}=g.\n\\]\nThe first relation says \\(r=4w+3\\). Since \\(w\\ge1\\), the possible red counts begin \\(7,11,15,\\ldots\\). At \\(r=7\\), the required blue count would be \\(5/3\\), which is impossible. At \\(r=11\\), all three counts are positive integers:\n\\[\nw=2,\\qquad b=3,\\qquad g=5.\n\\]\nAs \\(r\\) increases, each of these required counts increases, so this first feasible red count also gives the smallest total. It works because\n\\[\n\\binom{11}{4}\n=2\\binom{11}{3}\n=2\\cdot3\\binom{11}{2}\n=11\\cdot2\\cdot3\\cdot5\n=330.\n\\]\nThe smallest total is \\(11+2+3+5=\\boxed{21}\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{B}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
"sourceURL": "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/amc12/1996/solutions",
