"year": 1997,
"level": "AMC 8",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 8,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "Walter gets up at \\(6:30\\) a.m., catches the school bus at \\(7:30\\) a.m., has \\(6\\) classes that last \\(50\\) minutes each, has \\(30\\) minutes for lunch, and has \\(2\\) hours additional time at school. He takes the bus home and arrives at \\(4:00\\) p.m. How many minutes has he spent on the bus?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(30\\)",
"B": "\\(60\\)",
"C": "\\(75\\)",
"D": "\\(90\\)",
"E": "\\(120\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "B",
"solution": "Start at \\(7{:}30\\) a.m., when Walter boards the first bus. From then until \\(4{:}00\\) p.m. is \\(8\\) hours \\(30\\) minutes, or\n\\[\n8\\cdot60+30=510\\text{ minutes}.\n\\]\nThis interval consists of the two bus rides and his time at school.\n\nHis six classes take \\(6\\cdot50=300\\) minutes, and the additional two hours take \\(120\\) minutes. Including lunch, his school time is\n\\[\n300+30+120=450\\text{ minutes}.\n\\]\nTherefore, his total time on the bus is\n\\[\n510-450=60\\text{ minutes}.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(60\\) minutes, choice B.",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
