"question": "If \\(1998\\) is written as a product of two positive integers whose difference is as small as possible, then the difference is",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(8\\)",
"B": "\\(15\\)",
"C": "\\(17\\)",
"D": "\\(47\\)",
"E": "\\(93\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "C",
"solution": "Method 1: Find the largest possible smaller factor\n\nLet the two positive integer factors be \\(a\\le b\\). Since \\(ab=1998\\), we have \\(a^2\\le1998<45^2\\), so \\(a\\le44\\). As the smaller factor increases, the larger factor \\(b=1998/a\\) decreases, so their difference decreases. We therefore want the largest divisor of \\(1998\\) that is at most \\(44\\).\n\nThe prime factorization is\n\\[\n1998=2\\cdot3^3\\cdot37=54\\cdot37.\n\\]\nA divisor containing \\(37\\) can be at most \\(44\\) only if it is \\(37\\) itself, because even \\(2\\cdot37>44\\). A divisor not containing \\(37\\) must divide \\(54\\). Those divisors are\n\\[\n1,2,3,6,9,18,27,54.\n\\]\nOf these, \\(54\\) is too large, and all the others are smaller than \\(37\\). Thus the largest eligible smaller factor is \\(37\\), paired with \\(54\\). The minimum difference is\n\\[\n54-37=17,\n\\]\nchoice C.\n\nMethod 2: Bound the sum using parity\n\nLet \\(a\\le b\\) be positive integers with \\(ab=1998\\), and write \\(s=a+b\\). The identity\n\\[\n(b-a)^2=s^2-4ab\n\\]\nshows that a lower bound on the sum gives a lower bound on the difference.\n\nBecause \\(1998=2\\cdot999\\) is twice an odd number, exactly one of \\(a,b\\) is even. Thus \\(s\\) is odd. Also,\n\\[\ns^2=(b-a)^2+4ab\\ge7992>89^2.\n\\]\nSince \\(s\\) is positive, \\(s>89\\). The next possible odd integer is \\(91\\), so \\(s\\ge91\\). Consequently,\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n(b-a)^2&=s^2-7992\\\\\n&\\ge91^2-7992\\\\\n&=289=17^2.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nSince \\(b-a\\ge0\\), their difference is at least \\(17\\). The pair \\(37,54\\) has product \\(1998\\) and difference \\(17\\), so this bound is attained. The answer is \\(17\\), choice C.",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
