"year": 1998,
"level": "AMC 12",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 25,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "A piece of graph paper is folded once so that \\((0,2)\\) is matched with \\((4,0),\\) and \\((7,3)\\) is matched with \\((m,n).\\) Find \\(m+n.\\)",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(6.7\\)",
"B": "\\(6.8\\)",
"C": "\\(6.9\\)",
"D": "\\(7.0\\)",
"E": "\\(8.0\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "B",
"solution": "A fold reflects points across its crease, so the crease perpendicularly bisects every segment joining matched points. The given pair therefore determines the crease.\n\nThe midpoint of \\((0,2)\\) and \\((4,0)\\) is \\((2,1)\\), and their joining segment has slope\n\\[\n\\frac{0-2}{4-0}=-\\frac12.\n\\]\nThus the crease has slope \\(2\\) and equation\n\\[\ny-1=2(x-2),\\qquad y=2x-3.\n\\]\nLet \\(F\\) be the perpendicular foot from \\(P=(7,3)\\) to the crease. The line \\(PF\\) has slope \\(-1/2\\), so its equation is\n\\[\ny-3=-\\frac12(x-7).\n\\]\nAt its intersection with the crease,\n\\[\n2x-3=3-\\frac12(x-7),\n\\]\nwhich gives \\(5x=19\\). Hence\n\\[\nF=\\left(\\frac{19}{5},\\frac{23}{5}\\right).\n\\]\nBecause \\(F\\) is the midpoint of \\(P\\) and its reflected point \\((m,n)\\),\n\\[\nm=2\\cdot\\frac{19}{5}-7=\\frac35,\n\\qquad\nn=2\\cdot\\frac{23}{5}-3=\\frac{31}{5}.\n\\]\nTherefore \\(m+n=\\boxed{\\frac{34}{5}=6.8}\\), choice B.",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
"sourceURL": "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/amc12/1998/solutions",
