"level": "AMC 8",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 14,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "At Annville Junior High School, \\(30\\%\\) of the students in the Math Club are in the Science Club, and \\(80\\%\\) of the students in the Science Club are in the Math Club. There are \\(15\\) students in the Science Club. How many students are in the Math Club?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(12 \\)",
"B": "\\(15 \\)",
"C": "\\(30 \\)",
"D": "\\(36 \\)",
"E": "\\(40 \\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "E",
"solution": "Both percentages describe the same group: students who belong to both clubs. First use the Science Club's known membership to count that group. Since \\(80\\%\\) of its \\(15\\) students also belong to the Math Club, there are\n\\[\n0.80\\times15=12\n\\]\nstudents in both clubs.\n\nThese \\(12\\) students are \\(30\\%\\) of the Math Club. Dividing the known part by its percentage gives the whole membership:\n\\[\n12\\div0.30=40.\n\\]\nThe Math Club has \\(40\\) students, choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{E}}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
