"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "B",
"solution": "Method 1: Count the cubes that touch neither\n\nCounting cubes that avoid the sides and bottom prevents double counting cubes along edges or corners. Locate each cube by its row, column, and layer, numbered \\(1\\) through \\(4\\), with layer \\(1\\) at the bottom.\n\nTo avoid all four sides, a cube must be in row \\(2\\) or \\(3\\) and column \\(2\\) or \\(3\\). To avoid the bottom, it must be in layer \\(2,3,\\) or \\(4\\). Thus there are\n\\[\n2\\times2\\times3=12\n\\]\ncubes that touch none of the specified faces. Each choice of row, column, and layer identifies exactly one cube, so this includes every such cube once. The top layer is allowed because touching the top alone does not count.\n\nEvery other cube touches a side or the bottom. Their number is\n\\[\n64-12=\\boxed{52},\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\boxed{\\text{B}}\\).\n\nMethod 2: Count one horizontal layer at a time\n\nSeparate the cubes into their four horizontal layers. All \\(4\\times4=16\\) cubes in the bottom layer touch the bottom.\n\nIn each of the other three layers, count only cubes along the outside of its \\(4\\times4\\) array. Two complete outer rows contribute \\(4+4=8\\) cubes. In each of the two remaining rows, only the two end cubes touch a side, contributing another \\(2+2=4\\). Thus each upper layer contributes \\(8+4=12\\) cubes.\n\nThese groups do not overlap: different layers contain different cubes, and within an upper layer the complete outer rows are separate from the end cubes in the remaining rows. Every cube touching a side or the bottom belongs to one of these groups. The total is\n\\[\n16+3\\times12=\\boxed{52},\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\boxed{\\text{B}}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
"sourceURL": "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/amc8/1998/solutions",
