"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "E",
"solution": "A decrease of \\(25\\%\\) leaves \\(75\\%\\) of the original attendance, so the number of students attending is\n\\[\n108\\cdot0.75=81.\n\\]\nAt an average of two cookies per student, they need \\(81\\cdot2=162\\) cookies. Each full recipe makes \\(15\\) cookies, and\n\\[\n10\\cdot15=150<162,\\qquad 11\\cdot15=165\\ge162.\n\\]\nThus ten recipes fall short, while eleven provide enough. They should make \\(\\boxed{11}\\) recipes, choice \\(\\text{E}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
"sourceURL": "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/amc8/1999/solutions",
