"year": 2000,
"level": "AMC 10",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 3,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "Each day, Jenny ate \\(20\\%\\) of the jellybeans that were in her jar at the beginning of that day. At the end of the second day, \\(32\\) remained. How many jellybeans were in the jar originally?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(40\\)",
"B": "\\(50\\)",
"C": "\\(55\\)",
"D": "\\(60\\)",
"E": "\\(75\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "B",
"solution": "Eating \\(20\\%\\) leaves \\(80\\%=0.8\\) of the jellybeans present at the beginning of that day. To recover a day's starting amount, divide its ending amount by \\(0.8\\).\n\nThe \\(32\\) jellybeans left after the second day therefore came from\n\\[\n32\\div0.8=40\n\\]\njellybeans at the beginning of that day. Those \\(40\\) were left after the first day, so the original number was\n\\[\n40\\div0.8=50.\n\\]\nThus the jar originally contained \\(\\boxed{50}\\) jellybeans, choice \\(\\text{B}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
"sourceURL": "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/amc10/2000/solutions",
