"batch": "NA",
"number": 11,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "Two different prime numbers between \\(4\\) and \\(18\\) are chosen. When their sum is subtracted from their product, which of the following numbers could be obtained?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(21\\)",
"B": "\\(60\\)",
"C": "\\(119\\)",
"D": "\\(180\\)",
"E": "\\(231\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "C",
"solution": "The primes between \\(4\\) and \\(18\\) are \\(5,7,11,13,17\\). Write the chosen pair as \\(p<q\\). This lists each pair once because reversing the two primes does not change their sum or product.\n\nFor each smaller prime \\(p\\), use every larger prime from the list in increasing order. The resulting values of \\(pq-(p+q)\\) are\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\np=5 &: \\quad 23,39,47,63,\\\\\np=7 &: \\quad 59,71,95,\\\\\np=11 &: \\quad 119,159,\\\\\np=13 &: \\quad 191.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nThese cases exhaust all distinct pairs. Only \\(119\\) appears among the choices; specifically,\n\\[\n11\\cdot13-(11+13)=143-24=\\boxed{119}.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{C}}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
