"number": 3,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "Each day, Jenny ate \\(20\\%\\) of the jellybeans that were in her jar at the beginning of that day. At the end of the second day, \\(32\\) remained. How many jellybeans were in the jar originally?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(40\\)",
"B": "\\(50\\)",
"C": "\\(55\\)",
"D": "\\(60\\)",
"E": "\\(75\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "B",
"solution": "Eating \\(20\\%\\) leaves \\(80\\%=0.8\\) of the jellybeans present at the beginning of that day. To recover a day's starting amount from its remaining amount, divide by \\(0.8\\).\n\nThus the number at the beginning of the second day was\n\\[\n32\\div0.8=40.\n\\]\nThose \\(40\\) jellybeans were what remained after the first day, so the original number was\n\\[\n40\\div0.8=50.\n\\]\nStarting with \\(50\\), Jenny eats \\(10\\) on the first day and \\(8\\) on the second, leaving \\(32\\) as required. The answer is \\(\\boxed{50}\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{B}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
