"year": 2001,
"level": "AMC 10",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 8,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "Wanda, Darren, Beatrice, and Chi are tutors in the school math lab. Their schedule is as follows: Darren works every third school day, Wanda works every fourth school day, Beatrice works every sixth school day, and Chi works every seventh school day. Today they are all working in the math lab. In how many school days from today will they next be together tutoring in the lab?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(42\\)",
"B": "\\(84\\)",
"C": "\\(126\\)",
"D": "\\(178\\)",
"E": "\\(252\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "B",
"solution": "Count today as day \\(0\\). The next day when all four work must be a positive multiple of each schedule period: \\(3,4,6,7\\). We therefore need their least common multiple.\n\nThe factorizations \\(4=2^2\\) and \\(6=2\\cdot3\\) show that a common multiple must contain two factors of \\(2\\) and one factor of \\(3\\). It must also contain a factor of \\(7\\). The smallest such positive number is\n\\[\n2^2\\cdot3\\cdot7=84.\n\\]\nThis is divisible by \\(3,4,6,7\\), and every common multiple contains these required prime factors, so none smaller can work. They next tutor together in \\(\\boxed{84}\\) school days, choice B.",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
