"level": "AMC 10",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 9,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "The state income tax where Kristin lives is levied at the rate of \\(p\\%\\) of the first \\(\\$28000\\) of annual income plus \\((p+2)\\%\\) of any amount above \\(\\$28000.\\) Kristin noticed that the state income tax she paid amounted to \\((p+0.25)\\%\\) of her annual income. What was her annual income?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(\\$28000\\)",
"B": "\\(\\$32000\\)",
"C": "\\(\\$35000\\)",
"D": "\\(\\$42000\\)",
"E": "\\(\\$56000\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "B",
"solution": "Kristin's overall tax rate is greater than \\(p\\%\\), so her income must exceed \\(\\$28{,}000\\). Otherwise, all her income would be taxed at \\(p\\%\\).\n\nThink of her tax as \\(p\\%\\) of all her income, plus an extra \\(2\\%\\) of the part above \\(\\$28{,}000\\). This extra tax also equals \\(0.25\\%\\) of her total income. Since \\(2\\%\\) is eight times \\(0.25\\%\\), the higher-bracket income must be one eighth of her total income.\n\nThe remaining seven eighths, or \\(87.5\\%\\), equals \\(\\$28{,}000\\). Therefore her annual income was\n\\[\n28{,}000\\div0.875=32{,}000.\n\\]\nThis exceeds the bracket threshold, as required. Her annual income was \\(\\$32{,}000\\), choice B.",
