"year": 2002,
"level": "AMC 8",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 13,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "For his birthday, Bert gets a box that holds \\(125\\) jellybeans when filled to capacity. A few weeks later, Carrie gets a larger box full of jellybeans. Her box is twice as high, twice as wide and twice as long as Bert’s. Approximately, how many jellybeans did Carrie get?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(250\\)",
"B": "\\(500\\)",
"C": "\\(625\\)",
"D": "\\(750\\)",
"E": "\\(1000\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "E",
"solution": "Jellybeans fill space, so compare the boxes' volumes. A rectangular box's volume is its length times its width times its height. Doubling each dimension therefore multiplies the volume by\n\\[\n2\\cdot2\\cdot2=8.\n\\]\nAssuming comparable jellybean sizes and packing density in both boxes, Carrie receives approximately\n\\[\n125\\cdot8=1000\n\\]\njellybeans, choice \\(\\text{E}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
"sourceURL": "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/amc8/2002/solutions",
"figureSources": {},
