"year": 2002,
"level": "AMC 8",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 14,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "A merchant offers a large group of items at \\(30\\%\\) off. Later, the merchant takes \\(20\\%\\) off these sale prices and claims that the final price of these items is \\(50\\%\\) off the original price. The total discount is",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(35\\%\\)",
"B": "\\(44\\%\\)",
"C": "\\(50\\%\\)",
"D": "\\(56\\%\\)",
"E": "\\(60\\%\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "B",
"solution": "Track each \\(100\\) dollars of the original price. Since both discounts are proportional to the current price, the resulting percentage discount is the same for any positive original price. The first discount leaves \\(70\\) dollars. The second discount is \\(20\\%\\) of this sale price, so it removes\n\\[\n\\frac{20}{100}\\cdot70=14\n\\]\ndollars. The final price is \\(70-14=56\\) dollars, saving \\(100-56=44\\) dollars out of every \\(100\\). Thus the total discount is \\(44\\%\\), choice \\(\\text{B}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
"sourceURL": "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/amc8/2002/solutions",
