"year": 2003,
"level": "AMC 12",
"batch": "A",
"number": 2,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "Members of the Rockham Soccer League buy socks and T-shirts. Socks cost \\(\\$4\\) per pair and each T-shirt costs \\(\\$5\\) more than a pair of socks. Each member needs one pair of socks and a shirt for home games and another pair of socks and a shirt for away games. If the total cost is \\(\\$2366,\\) how many members are in the League?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(77\\)",
"B": "\\(91\\)",
"C": "\\(143\\)",
"D": "\\(182\\)",
"E": "\\(286\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "B",
"solution": "First find the clothing cost for one member, since every member needs the same items. A T-shirt costs \\(4+5=9\\) dollars, so one pair of socks and one shirt cost \\(4+9=13\\) dollars.\n\nEach member needs one such outfit for home games and another for away games. The cost per member is therefore \\(2\\cdot13=26\\) dollars. Dividing the total cost by this amount gives\n\\[\n\\frac{2366}{26}=91.\n\\]\nThus there are \\(\\boxed{91}\\) members, choice \\(\\mathrm{B}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
