"choices": {
"A": "\\(\\$7\\)",
"B": "\\(\\$14\\)",
"C": "\\(\\$19\\)",
"D": "\\(\\$20\\)",
"E": "\\(\\$39\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "D",
"solution": "Two weeks contain \\(14\\) days. Since Al takes one pill of each color daily, one green pill and one pink pill together cost\n\\[\n\\frac{546}{14}=39\\text{ dollars}.\n\\]\nA green pill costs one dollar more than a pink pill. Replacing the pink pill in this pair with another green pill therefore raises the cost to \\(39+1=40\\) dollars. Two green pills cost \\(40\\) dollars, so one costs \\(\\boxed{\\$20}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\).",
