"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "Blake and Jenny each took four \\(100\\)-point tests. Blake averaged \\(78\\) on the four tests. Jenny scored \\(10\\) points higher than Blake on the first test, \\(10\\) points lower than him on the second test, and \\(20\\) points higher on both the third and fourth tests. What is the difference between Jenny’s average and Blake’s average on these four tests?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(10\\)",
"B": "\\(15\\)",
"C": "\\(20\\)",
"D": "\\(25\\)",
"E": "\\(40\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "A",
"solution": "Jenny's \\(10\\)-point gain on the first test exactly offsets her \\(10\\)-point loss on the second. Her gains on the third and fourth tests therefore give her \\(20+20=40\\) more points in total.\n\nEach average is the total score divided by \\(4\\), so the difference between the averages is\n\\[\n40\\div4=10.\n\\]\nJenny's average is \\(10\\) points higher, choice \\(A\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
