"year": 2004,
"level": "AMC 10",
"batch": "A",
"number": 12,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "Henry’s Hamburger Heaven offers its hamburgers with the following condiments: ketchup, mustard, mayonnaise, tomato, lettuce, pickles, cheese, and onions. A customer can choose one, two, or three meat patties, and any collection of condiments. How many different kinds of hamburgers can be ordered?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(24\\)",
"B": "\\(256\\)",
"C": "\\(768\\)",
"D": "\\(40{,}320\\)",
"E": "\\(120{,}960\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "C",
"solution": "For each of the \\(8\\) condiments, the customer makes one of two choices: include it or leave it out. These choices can be made freely, giving\n\\[\n2^8=256\n\\]\ncollections of condiments. This includes choosing no condiments and choosing all eight.\n\nEach collection can accompany \\(1\\), \\(2\\), or \\(3\\) meat patties, so the total is\n\\[\n3\\cdot256=\\boxed{768}.\n\\]\nEvery hamburger has exactly one patty count and one set of include-or-omit choices, so every kind is counted once. The answer is choice \\(\\mathrm{C}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
