"level": "AMC 12",
"batch": "A",
"number": 4,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "Bertha has \\(6\\) daughters and no sons. Some of her daughters have \\(6\\) daughters, and the rest have none. Bertha has a total of \\(30\\) daughters and granddaughters, and no great-granddaughters. How many of Bertha’s daughters and granddaughters have no daughters?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(22\\)",
"B": "\\(23\\)",
"C": "\\(24\\)",
"D": "\\(25\\)",
"E": "\\(26\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "E",
"solution": "Separate the two generations first. Bertha has \\(6\\) daughters, so she has \\(30-6=24\\) granddaughters. Each daughter who has daughters has exactly \\(6\\), so\n\\[\n24\\div6=4\n\\]\nof Bertha's daughters have daughters.\n\nNone of her granddaughters has a daughter, since such a daughter would be Bertha's great-granddaughter. Thus exactly \\(4\\) of the \\(30\\) daughters and granddaughters have daughters. The number with no daughters is\n\\[\n30-4=26,\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\mathrm{E}\\).",
