"level": "AMC 12",
"batch": "B",
"number": 6,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "Minneapolis-St. Paul International Airport is \\(8\\) miles southwest of downtown St. Paul and \\(10\\) miles southeast of downtown Minneapolis. Which of the following is closest to the number of miles between downtown St. Paul and downtown Minneapolis?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(13\\)",
"B": "\\(14\\)",
"C": "\\(15\\)",
"D": "\\(16\\)",
"E": "\\(17\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "A",
"solution": "Let \\(A\\) be the airport, \\(S\\) downtown St. Paul, and \\(M\\) downtown Minneapolis. Since the airport is southwest of St. Paul, \\(S\\) is northeast of \\(A\\). Similarly, \\(M\\) is northwest of \\(A\\). Northeast and northwest differ by \\(90^\\circ\\), so \\(\\triangle SAM\\) is a right triangle with legs \\(AS=8\\) and \\(AM=10\\).\n\nThe Pythagorean theorem gives the distance between the downtowns:\n\\[\nSM=\\sqrt{8^2+10^2}=\\sqrt{164}.\n\\]\nBecause \\(12^2<164<13^2\\), this distance is between \\(12\\) and \\(13\\) miles. Every answer choice is at least \\(13\\), so the closest choice is \\(13\\) miles, choice A.",
