"year": 2004,
"level": "AMC 8",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 10,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "Handy Aaron helped a neighbor \\(1 \\frac{1}{4}\\) hours on Monday, \\(50\\) minutes on Tuesday, from \\(8:20\\) to \\(10:45\\) on Wednesday morning, and a half-hour on Friday. He is paid \\(\\$3\\) per hour. How much did he earn for the week?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(\\$8\\)",
"B": "\\(\\$9\\)",
"C": "\\(\\$10\\)",
"D": "\\(\\$12\\)",
"E": "\\(\\$15\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "E",
"solution": "Put all the work times in minutes so they can be added. There are \\(60\\) minutes in an hour, so Monday's \\(1\\frac14\\) hours is \\(60+60\\div4=75\\) minutes. Friday's half-hour is \\(30\\) minutes.\n\nOn Wednesday, \\(8{:}20\\) to \\(10{:}20\\) is two hours, followed by another \\(25\\) minutes to \\(10{:}45\\). Thus Wednesday's work lasted \\(2\\times60+25=145\\) minutes.\n\nThe week's total is\n\\[\n75+50+145+30=300\\text{ minutes}.\n\\]\nSince \\(300\\div60=5\\), Aaron worked \\(5\\) hours. At \\(\\$3\\) per hour, he earned \\(5\\times\\$3=\\$15\\), choice E.",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
