"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "What is the area enclosed by the graph of \\(|3x| + |4y| = 12?\\)",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(6\\)",
"B": "\\(12\\)",
"C": "\\(16\\)",
"D": "\\(24\\)",
"E": "\\(25\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "D",
"solution": "In the first quadrant, where \\(x,y\\geq0\\), the equation becomes\n\\[\n3x+4y=12.\n\\]\nIts portion in that quadrant is the line segment joining \\((4,0)\\) and \\((0,3)\\). Together with the axes, it bounds a right triangle with legs \\(4\\) and \\(3\\).\n\nChanging the sign of either coordinate leaves the original absolute-value equation unchanged. Reflecting the first segment across the axes therefore gives the other three sides of the boundary. The enclosed region consists of four congruent right triangles whose interiors do not overlap. Its area is\n\\[\n4\\left(\\frac12\\cdot4\\cdot3\\right)=\\boxed{24},\n\\]\nwhich is choice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
