"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "B",
"solution": "The percentage scoring \\(95\\) is\n\\[\n100\\%-10\\%-25\\%-20\\%-15\\%=30\\%.\n\\]\nTo find the mean, weight each score by the fraction of students who earned it:\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{mean}\n&=0.10(70)+0.25(80)+0.20(85)\\\\\n&\\quad+0.15(90)+0.30(95)\\\\\n&=7+20+17+13.5+28.5\\\\\n&=86.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nFor the median, imagine the scores sorted from least to greatest. The first \\(10\\%+25\\%=35\\%\\) are below \\(85\\), and the next \\(20\\%\\) equal \\(85\\). Thus the middle positions lie in the group scoring \\(85\\), so the median is \\(85\\).\n\nThe difference is \\(86-85=\\boxed{1}\\) point, choice \\(\\mathrm{B}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
