"year": 2005,
"level": "AMC 8",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 11,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "The sales tax rate in Bergville is \\(6\\%\\). During a sale at the Bergville Coat Closet, the price of a coat is discounted \\(20\\%\\) from its \\(\\$90.00\\) price. Two clerks, Jack and Jill, calculate the bill independently. Jack rings up \\(\\$90.00\\) and adds \\(6\\%\\) sales tax, then subtracts \\(20\\%\\) from this total. Jill rings up \\(\\$90.00\\), subtracts \\(20\\%\\) of the price, then adds \\(6\\%\\) of the discounted price for sales tax. What is Jack’s total minus Jill’s total?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(-\\$ 1.06\\)",
"B": "\\(-\\$ 0.53\\)",
"C": "\\(\\$ 0\\)",
"D": "\\(\\$ 0.53\\)",
"E": "\\(\\$ 1.06\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "C",
"solution": "Adding \\(6\\%\\) tax means paying \\(106\\%\\) of the current amount, so it multiplies that amount by \\(1.06\\). A \\(20\\%\\) discount leaves \\(80\\%\\), so it multiplies the current amount by \\(0.80\\).\n\nJack's total is \\(90\\times1.06\\times0.80\\) dollars. Jill's total is \\(90\\times0.80\\times1.06\\) dollars. Changing the order of the factors does not change their product, so the two totals are equal.\n\nJack's total minus Jill's total is therefore \\(\\boxed{\\$0}\\), choice \\(\\text{C}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
"sourceURL": "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/amc8/2005/solutions",
