"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "E",
"solution": "An am/pm display uses hours \\(1\\) through \\(12\\). Among hours \\(1\\) through \\(9\\), the largest digit sum is \\(9\\). The remaining hours, \\(10,11,12\\), have digit sums \\(1,2,3\\), so no hour contributes more than \\(9\\).\n\nMinutes run from \\(00\\) through \\(59\\), so their tens digit is at most \\(5\\) and their ones digit is at most \\(9\\). Thus the minute digits sum to at most \\(14\\).\n\nEvery display consequently has digit sum at most \\(9+14=23\\). The valid time \\(9{:}59\\), either am or pm, attains this bound:\n\\[\n9+5+9=23.\n\\]\nThe largest possible sum is \\(\\boxed{23}\\), choice E.",
