"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "C",
"solution": "Expanding the square reveals which coordinate pairs satisfy the equation:\n\\[\nx^2+2xy+y^2=x^2+y^2\n\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad xy=0.\n\\]\nIf \\(x=0\\), every real value of \\(y\\) works. If \\(x\\ne0\\), dividing by \\(x\\) gives \\(y=0\\). Conversely, either coordinate being zero makes the original equation true.\n\nThus the graph consists exactly of \\(x=0\\), the \\(y\\)-axis, and \\(y=0\\), the \\(x\\)-axis. These are two lines, so the answer is \\(\\boxed{\\text{C}}\\).",
