"year": 2006,
"level": "AMC 10",
"batch": "B",
"number": 11,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "What is the tens digit in the sum \\(7! + 8! + 9! + \\cdots + 2006!\\,?\\)",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(1\\)",
"B": "\\(3\\)",
"C": "\\(4\\)",
"D": "\\(6\\)",
"E": "\\(9\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "C",
"solution": "Adding a multiple of \\(100\\) changes neither the tens digit nor the ones digit, so we only need the last two digits of each term.\n\nRecall that \\(n!=1\\cdot2\\cdots n\\). For every \\(n\\ge10\\), this product contains the distinct factors \\(2,5,10\\), whose product is \\(100\\). Thus every term from \\(10!\\) through \\(2006!\\) is a multiple of \\(100\\) and does not affect the requested digit.\n\nThe remaining terms are\n\\[\n7!=5040,\\qquad 8!=40320,\\qquad 9!=362880.\n\\]\nTheir last two digits contribute\n\\[\n40+20+80=140.\n\\]\nTherefore the complete sum ends in \\(40\\), and its tens digit is \\(\\boxed{4}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{C}}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
