"question": "Circles with centers at \\(O\\) and \\(P\\) have radii \\(2\\) and \\(4,\\) respectively, and are externally tangent. Points \\(A\\) and \\(B\\) on the circle with center \\(O\\) and points \\(C\\) and \\(D\\) on the circle with center \\(P\\) are such that \\(\\overline{AD}\\) and \\(\\overline{BC}\\) are common external tangents to the circles. What is the area of the concave hexagon \\(AOBCPD?\\)\n\n[Figure 1](figures/2006_AMC_10B_Q24_question_fig1.svg)",
