"year": 2006,
"level": "AMC 12",
"batch": "A",
"number": 4,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "A digital watch displays hours and minutes with AM and PM. What is the largest possible sum of the digits in the display?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(17\\)",
"B": "\\(19\\)",
"C": "\\(21\\)",
"D": "\\(22\\)",
"E": "\\(23\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "E",
"solution": "With AM and PM, the displayed hour ranges from \\(1\\) through \\(12\\). Hours \\(1\\) through \\(9\\) have digit sum at most \\(9\\), while \\(10,11,12\\) have digit sums \\(1,2,3\\). Thus the largest hour contribution is \\(9\\).\n\nThe minutes range from \\(00\\) through \\(59\\). Their tens digit is at most \\(5\\), and their ones digit is at most \\(9\\), so their digit sum is at most \\(14\\).\n\nEvery display therefore has digit sum at most\n\\[\n9+14=23.\n\\]\nThe valid display \\(9{:}59\\) AM attains this bound. A leading zero, if displayed, contributes nothing. The largest sum is \\(\\boxed{23}\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{E}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
