"level": "AMC 12",
"batch": "B",
"number": 6,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "Francesca uses \\(100\\) grams of lemon juice, \\(100\\) grams of sugar, and \\(400\\) grams of water to make lemonade. There are \\(25\\) calories in \\(100\\) grams of lemon juice and \\(386\\) calories in \\(100\\) grams of sugar. Water contains no calories. How many calories are in \\(200\\) grams of her lemonade?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(129\\)",
"B": "\\(137\\)",
"C": "\\(174\\)",
"D": "\\(223\\)",
"E": "\\(411\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "B",
"solution": "First find the mass and calories of the whole batch. Its mass is\n\\[\n100+100+400=600\\text{ grams},\n\\]\nand its calorie total is \\(25+386=411\\), since water contributes none.\n\nThe batch makes three equal \\(200\\)-gram servings. Each serving of the mixed lemonade has one-third of the batch's calories, so it contains\n\\[\n411\\div3=137\\text{ calories}.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(137\\) calories, choice B.",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
