"batch": "B",
"number": 7,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "Mr. and Mrs. Lopez have two children. When they get into their family car, two people sit in the front, and the other two sit in the back. Either Mr. Lopez or Mrs. Lopez must sit in the driver’s seat. How many seating arrangements are possible?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(4\\)",
"B": "\\(12\\)",
"C": "\\(16\\)",
"D": "\\(24\\)",
"E": "\\(48\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "B",
"solution": "Choose the driver first so that the driving restriction is satisfied immediately. There are \\(2\\) choices, Mr. Lopez or Mrs. Lopez. Once the driver is chosen, there are \\(3\\) choices for the front passenger, \\(2\\) choices for the left back seat, and \\(1\\) person left for the right back seat. Thus the number of arrangements is\n\\[\n2\\cdot3\\cdot2\\cdot1=12.\n\\]\nEvery permitted arrangement specifies exactly one sequence of these choices, so all arrangements are included once. The answer is \\(12\\), choice B.",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
