"year": 2006,
"level": "AMC 8",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 20,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "A singles tournament had six players. Each player played every other player only once, with no ties. If Helen won \\(4\\) games, Ines won \\(3\\) games, Janet won \\(2\\) games, Kendra won \\(2\\) games and Lara won \\(2\\) games, how many games did Monica win?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(0\\)",
"B": "\\(1\\)",
"C": "\\(2\\)",
"D": "\\(3\\)",
"E": "\\(4\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "C",
"solution": "Each of the six players plays five games, one against each other player. Thus there are \\(6\\cdot5=30\\) player appearances in games. Each game has two players, so this counts every game exactly twice. The number of games is therefore\n\\[\n\\frac{6\\cdot5}{2}=15.\n\\]\nBecause there are no ties, each game contributes exactly one win. The five listed players won\n\\[\n4+3+2+2+2=13\n\\]\ngames altogether. Monica must have won the remaining \\(15-13=\\boxed{2}\\) games, choice \\(\\mathrm{C}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
"sourceURL": "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/amc8/2006/solutions",
