"year": 2007,
"level": "AMC 10",
"batch": "B",
"number": 16,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "A teacher gave a test to a class in which \\(10\\%\\) of the students are juniors and \\(90\\%\\) are seniors. The average score on the test was \\(84.\\) The juniors all received the same score, and the average score of the seniors was \\(83.\\) What score did each of the juniors receive on the test?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(85\\)",
"B": "\\(88\\)",
"C": "\\(93\\)",
"D": "\\(94\\)",
"E": "\\(98\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "C",
"solution": "The group averages must be weighted by the fractions of the class in each group. Let \\(x\\) be the common junior score. Since juniors make up \\(\\frac{1}{10}\\) of the class and seniors make up \\(\\frac{9}{10}\\),\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{10}x+\\frac{9}{10}\\cdot83=84.\n\\]\nMultiplying by \\(10\\) gives \\(x+747=840\\), so \\(x=93\\). Thus each junior received \\(93\\), choice \\(C\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
"sourceURL": "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/amc10/2007B/solutions",
