"batch": "A",
"number": 7,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "The fraction\n\n\\[ \\dfrac{\\left(3^{2008}\\right)^2 - \\left(3^{2006}\\right)^2}{\\left(3^{2007}\\right)^2 - \\left(3^{2005}\\right)^2} \\]\n\nsimplifies to which of the following?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(1\\)",
"B": "\\(\\dfrac{9}{4}\\)",
"C": "\\(3\\)",
"D": "\\(\\dfrac{9}{2}\\)",
"E": "\\(9\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "E",
"solution": "Increasing an exponent of \\(3\\) by \\(1\\) multiplies the power by \\(3\\). Consequently, each quantity being squared in the numerator is three times the matching quantity in the denominator. Squaring multiplies each matching term by \\(3^2=9\\).\n\nLet\n\\[\nd=(3^{2007})^2-(3^{2005})^2.\n\\]\nBecause \\(3^{2007}>3^{2005}>0\\), we have \\(d>0\\). The numerator is\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n(3^{2008})^2-(3^{2006})^2\n&=9(3^{2007})^2-9(3^{2005})^2\\\\\n&=9d.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nThus the fraction is \\(\\frac{9d}{d}=9\\), with cancellation valid because \\(d\\ne0\\). The answer is \\(9\\), choice \\(E\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
"sourceURL": "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/amc10/2008A/solutions",
