"year": 2008,
"level": "AMC 10",
"batch": "B",
"number": 4,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "A semipro baseball league has teams with \\(21\\) players each. League rules state that a player must be paid at least \\(\\$15{,}000,\\) and that the total of all players’ salaries for each team cannot exceed \\(\\$700{,}000.\\) What is the maximum possible salary, in dollars, for a single player?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(270{,}000\\)",
"B": "\\(385{,}000\\)",
"C": "\\(400{,}000\\)",
"D": "\\(430{,}000\\)",
"E": "\\(700{,}000\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "C",
"solution": "To maximize one player's salary, first reserve the minimum amount owed to everyone else. There are \\(21-1=20\\) other players, whose combined salaries must be at least\n\\[\n20\\cdot15{,}000=300{,}000\n\\]\ndollars. Therefore the chosen player's salary cannot exceed\n\\[\n700{,}000-300{,}000=400{,}000\n\\]\ndollars.\n\nThis bound is attainable: pay one player \\(400{,}000\\) dollars and each of the other players \\(15{,}000\\) dollars. Every player receives at least the minimum, and the total is exactly \\(700{,}000\\) dollars. Thus the maximum salary is \\(400{,}000\\) dollars, choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{C}}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
