"question": "Older television screens have an aspect ratio of \\(4:3.\\) That is, the ratio of the width to the height is \\(4:3.\\) The aspect ratio of many movies is not \\(4:3,\\) so they are sometimes shown on a television screen by “letterboxing” — darkening strips of equal height at the top and bottom of the screen, as shown. Suppose a movie has an aspect ratio of \\(2:1\\) and is shown on an older television screen with a \\(27\\)-inch diagonal. What is the height, in inches, of each darkened strip?\n\n[Figure 1](figures/2008_AMC_12A_Q09_question_fig1.svg)",
