"year": 2008,
"level": "AMC 12",
"batch": "A",
"number": 14,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "What is the area of the region defined by the inequality \\[|3x - 18| + |2y + 7| \\le 3?\\]",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(3\\)",
"B": "\\(\\dfrac{7}{2}\\)",
"C": "\\(4\\)",
"D": "\\(\\dfrac{9}{2}\\)",
"E": "\\(5\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "A",
"solution": "The absolute values measure horizontal and vertical distances from \\((6,-7/2)\\). Recenter the coordinates by setting \\(u=x-6\\) and \\(v=y+7/2\\). This translates the region without changing its area, and the inequality becomes\n\\[\n3|u|+2|v|\\le 3.\n\\]\nIn the first quadrant, this is \\(3u+2v\\le3\\), so the region there is the right triangle with vertices \\((0,0)\\), \\((1,0)\\), and \\((0,3/2)\\). Changing either coordinate's sign leaves the inequality unchanged, so the other three quadrants contain reflected copies of this triangle.\n\nThese four triangles cover the entire region, and their interiors do not overlap. Their shared edges contribute no area. Consequently, the total area is\n\\[\n4\\left(\\frac12\\cdot1\\cdot\\frac32\\right)=\\boxed{3},\n\\]\nchoice A.",
