"level": "AMC 8",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 9,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "In \\(2005\\) Tycoon Tammy invested \\(\\$100\\) for two years. During the first year her investment suffered a \\(15\\%\\) loss, but during the second year the remaining investment showed a \\(20\\%\\) gain. Over the two-year period, what was the change in Tammy’s investment?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(5\\%\\) loss",
"B": "\\(2\\%\\) loss",
"C": "\\(1\\%\\) gain",
"D": "\\(2\\%\\) gain",
"E": "\\(5\\%\\) gain"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "D",
"solution": "The second year's gain is based on the money remaining after the first year's loss. The first-year loss is \\(0.15\\times100=15\\) dollars, leaving \\(100-15=85\\) dollars. The second-year gain is \\(0.20\\times85=17\\) dollars, so the final investment is \\(85+17=102\\) dollars.\n\nCompared with the original investment, the percentage increase is\n\\[\n\\frac{102-100}{100}\\times100\\%=2\\%.\n\\]\nThus Tammy's investment showed a \\(2\\%\\) gain, choice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
