"level": "AMC 8",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 13,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "Mr. Harman needs to know the combined weight in pounds of three boxes he wants to mail. However, the only available scale is not accurate for weights less than \\(100\\) pounds or more than \\(150\\) pounds. So the boxes are weighed in pairs in every possible way. The results are \\(122,\\) \\(125\\) and \\(127\\) pounds. What is the combined weight in pounds of the three boxes?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\( \\ 160 \\)",
"B": "\\( \\ 170 \\)",
"C": "\\( \\ 187 \\)",
"D": "\\( \\ 195 \\)",
"E": "\\( \\ 354 \\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "C",
"solution": "All three pair weights are within the scale's accurate range. Adding these weights is useful because each box was weighed with each of the other two boxes. Thus every box's weight appears exactly twice in the sum of the three readings.\n\nThe combined weight of the boxes is therefore half that sum:\n\\[\n\\frac{122+125+127}{2}\n=\\frac{374}{2}\n=187\\text{ pounds}.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(187\\) pounds, choice \\(\\mathrm{C}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
