"year": 2009,
"level": "AMC 12",
"batch": "A",
"number": 7,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "The first three terms of an arithmetic sequence are \\(2x - 3,\\) \\(5x - 11,\\) and \\(3x + 1\\) respectively. The \\(n\\)th term of the sequence is \\(2009.\\) What is \\(n?\\)",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(255\\)",
"B": "\\(502\\)",
"C": "\\(1004\\)",
"D": "\\(1506\\)",
"E": "\\(8037\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "B",
"solution": "Consecutive terms of an arithmetic sequence have equal differences. Applying this to the three given terms determines \\(x\\):\n\\[\n(5x-11)-(2x-3)=(3x+1)-(5x-11).\n\\]\nSimplifying gives\n\\[\n3x-8=-2x+12,\n\\qquad 5x=20,\n\\qquad x=4.\n\\]\nThe first three terms are therefore \\(5,9,13\\), so the first term is \\(5\\) and the common difference is \\(4\\).\n\nFrom the first term to the \\(n\\)th term there are \\(n-1\\) increases of \\(4\\). Hence\n\\[\n5+4(n-1)=2009.\n\\]\nThus \\(n-1=2004/4=501\\), giving the positive integer index \\(n=502\\). The answer is \\(502\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{B}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
"sourceURL": "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/amc12/2009A/solutions",
