"year": 2009,
"level": "AMC 8",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 21,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "Andy and Bethany have a rectangular array of numbers with \\(40\\) rows and \\(75\\) columns. Andy adds the numbers in each row. The average of his \\(40\\) sums is \\(A.\\) Bethany adds the numbers in each column. The average of her \\(75\\) sums is \\(B.\\) What is the value of \\(\\dfrac{A}{B}?\\)",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(\\dfrac{64}{225}\\)",
"B": "\\(\\dfrac{8}{15}\\)",
"C": "\\(1\\)",
"D": "\\(\\dfrac{15}{8}\\)",
"E": "\\(\\dfrac{225}{64}\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "D",
"solution": "Both collections of sums have the same total: adding all row sums counts each entry exactly once, and adding all column sums does too. Let \\(S\\) be this common total. Using mean equals total divided by the number of values gives\n\\[\nA=\\frac{S}{40},\\qquad B=\\frac{S}{75}.\n\\]\nIf \\(S\\ne0\\), then \\(B\\ne0\\), and we may compute\n\\[\n\\frac{A}{B}\n=\\frac{S/40}{S/75}\n=\\frac{75}{40}\n=\\frac{15}{8}.\n\\]\nThis is choice \\(\\text{D}\\) whenever the requested ratio is defined.\n\nHowever, the statement does not require \\(S\\ne0\\). For example, an array containing only zeros has \\(A=B=0\\), making \\(A/B=0/0\\) undefined. Thus the answer is conditionally \\(\\boxed{\\frac{15}{8}}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\), but a nonzero-total condition is needed for an unconditional numerical answer.",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
