"year": 2010,
"level": "AMC 10",
"batch": "A",
"number": 8,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "Tony works \\(2\\) hours a day and is paid \\(\\$0.50\\) per hour for each full year of his age. During a six month period Tony worked \\(50\\) days and earned \\(\\$630.\\) How old was Tony at the end of the six month period?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(9\\)",
"B": "\\(11\\)",
"C": "\\(12\\)",
"D": "\\(13\\)",
"E": "\\(14\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "D",
"solution": "Working two hours makes Tony's daily pay numerically equal to his age in completed years: at age \\(n\\), he earns \\(2(0.50)n=n\\) dollars per working day.\n\nLet \\(N\\) be his age in completed years at the end of the period. In six months he can have at most one birthday, so his age on each working day was either \\(N-1\\) or \\(N\\). Therefore his earnings satisfy\n\\[\n50(N-1)\\le 630\\le 50N.\n\\]\nDividing by \\(50\\) and rearranging gives\n\\[\n12.6\\le N\\le 13.6.\n\\]\nSince \\(N\\) is an integer, \\(N=13\\). These earnings are possible: \\(20\\) days at \\(12\\) dollars and \\(30\\) days at \\(13\\) dollars give \\(20(12)+30(13)=630\\). Tony was \\(13\\) years old at the end, choice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
"sourceURL": "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/amc10/2010A/solutions",
