"level": "AMC 10",
"batch": "A",
"number": 10,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "Marvin had a birthday on Tuesday, May \\(27\\) in the leap year \\(2008.\\) In what year will his birthday next fall on a Saturday?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(2011\\)",
"B": "\\(2012\\)",
"C": "\\(2013\\)",
"D": "\\(2015\\)",
"E": "\\(2017\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "E",
"solution": "A year of \\(365\\) days contains \\(52\\) full weeks and one extra day, so the birthday usually moves forward one weekday. An interval containing February \\(29\\) has \\(366\\) days and moves it forward two weekdays.\n\nMay \\(27\\) comes after February \\(29\\), so the leap day of \\(2008\\) has already passed. The two-day shifts occur when moving into \\(2012\\) and \\(2016\\), the next leap years.\n\nStarting from Tuesday in \\(2008\\), the birthdays fall on Wednesday in \\(2009\\), Thursday in \\(2010\\), Friday in \\(2011\\), and Sunday in \\(2012\\).\n\nThey then fall on Monday in \\(2013\\), Tuesday in \\(2014\\), Wednesday in \\(2015\\), Friday in \\(2016\\), and Saturday in \\(2017\\).\n\nEvery intervening year has been checked, so the next Saturday birthday is in \\(2017\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{E}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
