"level": "AMC 10",
"batch": "B",
"number": 3,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "A drawer contains red, green, blue, and white socks with at least \\(2\\) of each color. What is the minimum number of socks that must be pulled from the drawer to guarantee a matching pair?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(3\\)",
"B": "\\(4\\)",
"C": "\\(5\\)",
"D": "\\(8\\)",
"E": "\\(9\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "C",
"solution": "It is possible to pull four socks with no matching pair by getting one of each color. Thus four socks do not guarantee a match.\n\nWith five socks, avoiding a match would require five different colors, but the drawer contains only four colors. Therefore any five socks include two of the same color. The minimum is \\(\\boxed{5}\\), choice \\(\\text{C}\\).",
