"year": 2010,
"level": "AMC 12",
"batch": "A",
"number": 2,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "A ferry boat shuttles tourists to an island every hour starting at \\(10\\) am until its last trip, which starts at \\(3\\) pm. One day the boat captain notes that on the \\(10\\) am trip there were \\(100\\) tourists on the ferry boat, and that on each successive trip, the number of tourists was \\(1\\) fewer than on the previous trip. How many tourists did the ferry take to the island that day?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(585\\)",
"B": "\\(594\\)",
"C": "\\(672\\)",
"D": "\\(679\\)",
"E": "\\(694\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "A",
"solution": "Include both the first and last departures: the ferry leaves at \\(10,11,12,1,2,3\\), so there are six trips. Their passenger counts are \\(100,99,98,97,96,95\\).\n\nPairing the first count with the last, the second with the next-to-last, and the two middle counts gives\n\\[\n(100+95)+(99+96)+(98+97)\n=3\\cdot195=\\boxed{585}.\n\\]\nThus the answer is choice \\(\\mathrm{A}\\).",
