"question": "What is the sum of the mean, median, and mode of the numbers \\(2,\\) \\(3,\\) \\(0,\\) \\(3,\\) \\(1,\\) \\(4,\\) \\(0,\\) \\(3?\\)",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\( \\ 6.5 \\)",
"B": "\\( \\ 7 \\)",
"C": "\\( \\ 7.5 \\)",
"D": "\\( \\ 8.5 \\)",
"E": "\\( \\ 9 \\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "C",
"solution": "The eight numbers have sum 16, so their mean is\n\\[\n\\frac{16}{8}=2.\n\\]\nTo find the median and mode, arrange the numbers in increasing order:\n\\[\n0,0,1,2,3,3,3,4.\n\\]\nWith eight values, the median is the average of the fourth and fifth values:\n\\[\n\\frac{2+3}{2}=2.5.\n\\]\nThe mode is 3, which occurs three times, more often than any other value. Therefore the requested sum is\n\\[\n2+2.5+3=\\boxed{7.5},\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\mathrm{C}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
