"batch": "B",
"number": 7,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "The sum of two angles of a triangle is \\(\\frac{6}{5}\\) of a right angle, and one of these two angles is \\(30^{\\circ}\\) larger than the other. What is the degree measure of the largest angle in the triangle?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(69 \\)",
"B": "\\(72 \\)",
"C": "\\(90 \\)",
"D": "\\(102 \\)",
"E": "\\(108 \\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "B",
"solution": "The largest angle need not be one of the specified two, so find all three. A right angle measures \\(90^\\circ\\), making the given pair's sum\n\\[\n\\frac65\\cdot90^\\circ=108^\\circ.\n\\]\nSubtracting the extra \\(30^\\circ\\) from the larger of these two leaves two equal copies of the smaller angle. Thus the smaller angle is \\((108^\\circ-30^\\circ)/2=39^\\circ\\), and the larger is \\(39^\\circ+30^\\circ=69^\\circ\\). The triangle's third angle is\n\\[\n180^\\circ-108^\\circ=72^\\circ.\n\\]\nSince \\(72>69>39\\), the largest angle is \\(72^\\circ\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{B}\\).",
