"batch": "B",
"number": 8,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "At a certain beach if it is at least \\(80^{\\circ} F\\) and sunny, then the beach will be crowded. On June \\(10\\) the beach was not crowded. What can be concluded about the weather conditions on June \\(10?\\)",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "The temperature was cooler than \\( 80^{\\circ} \\)F and it was\nnot sunny.",
"B": "The temperature was cooler than \\( 80^{\\circ}\n\\)F or it was not sunny.",
"C": "If the temperature was at least \\( 80^{\\circ}\\) F, then it was\nsunny.",
"D": "If the temperature was cooler than \\( 80^{\\circ}\\) F, then it\nwas sunny.",
"E": "If the temperature was cooler than \\( 80^{\\circ} \\)F, then it\nwas not sunny."
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "B",
"solution": "If June \\(10\\) had been both at least \\(80^\\circ\\mathrm{F}\\) and sunny, the given rule would force the beach to be crowded. This contradicts the information that it was not crowded. Therefore at least one of those weather conditions failed: the temperature was cooler than \\(80^\\circ\\mathrm{F}\\), or it was not sunny.\n\nHere “or” allows both conditions to fail. The information does not tell us which one failed or require both to fail. The conclusion is choice \\(\\mathrm{B}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
