"year": 2011,
"level": "AMC 12",
"batch": "B",
"number": 3,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "LeRoy and Bernardo went on a week-long trip together and agreed to share the costs equally. Over the week, each of them paid for various joint expenses such as gasoline and car rental. At the end of the trip it turned out that LeRoy had paid \\(A\\) dollars and Bernardo had paid \\(B\\) dollars, where \\(A \\lt B.\\) How many dollars must LeRoy give to Bernardo so that they share the costs equally?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(\\dfrac{A+B}{2}\\)",
"B": "\\(\\dfrac{A-B}{2}\\)",
"C": "\\(\\dfrac{B-A}{2}\\)",
"D": "\\(B-A\\)",
"E": "\\(A+B\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "C",
"solution": "Their total joint expense is \\(A+B\\), so each person's share is \\((A+B)/2\\). LeRoy has already paid \\(A\\), leaving\n\\[\n\\frac{A+B}{2}-A=\\boxed{\\frac{B-A}{2}}\n\\]\nfor him to give Bernardo. This amount is positive because \\(A<B\\). After the transfer, Bernardo's net cost is also\n\\[\nB-\\frac{B-A}{2}=\\frac{A+B}{2},\n\\]\nso the costs are shared equally. The answer is choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{C}}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
