"year": 2011,
"level": "AMC 12",
"batch": "B",
"number": 5,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "Let \\(N\\) be the second smallest positive integer that is divisible by every positive integer less than \\(7.\\) What is the sum of the digits of \\(N?\\)",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(3\\)",
"B": "\\(4\\)",
"C": "\\(5\\)",
"D": "\\(6\\)",
"E": "\\(9\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "A",
"solution": "A number divisible by every positive integer less than \\(7\\) must be divisible by \\(1,2,3,4,5,6\\). The required prime factors are two factors of \\(2\\) from \\(4\\), one factor of \\(3\\), and one factor of \\(5\\). Thus their least common multiple is\n\\[\n2^2\\cdot3\\cdot5=60.\n\\]\nEvery qualifying number is a multiple of \\(60\\), and every multiple of \\(60\\) is divisible by all six numbers. The first two positive possibilities are therefore \\(60\\) and \\(120\\). Hence \\(N=120\\), and its digit sum is\n\\[\n1+2+0=\\boxed{3}.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{A}}\\).",
