"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "B",
"solution": "Start numbering rows at a corner, which is black. In each odd-numbered row, the \\(31\\) squares alternate from black to black, giving \\(16\\) black squares and \\(15\\) red squares. In each even-numbered row, the colors are reversed, giving \\(15\\) black squares.\n\nAmong \\(31\\) rows there are \\(16\\) odd-numbered rows and \\(15\\) even-numbered rows. Every black square lies in exactly one of these rows, so the total is\n\\[\n16\\cdot16+15\\cdot15=256+225=\\boxed{481}.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice B.",
