"level": "AMC 10",
"batch": "B",
"number": 6,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "In order to estimate the value of \\(x-y\\) where \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) are real numbers with \\(x > y > 0,\\) Xiaoli rounded \\(x\\) up by a small amount, rounded \\(y\\) down by the same amount, and then subtracted her rounded values.\n\nWhich of the following statements is necessarily correct?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "Her estimate is larger than \\(x-y\\)",
"B": "Her estimate is smaller than \\( x-y \\)",
"C": "Her estimate equals \\(x-y \\)",
"D": "Her estimate equals \\( y-x \\)",
"E": "Her estimate is \\( 0 \\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "A",
"solution": "To track both rounding changes, let \\(t>0\\) be their common amount. The rounded values are \\(x+t\\) and \\(y-t\\), so Xiaoli's estimate \\(E\\) is\n\\[E=(x+t)-(y-t)=x-y+2t.\\]\nSubtracting \\(y-t\\) contributes another \\(+t\\), so the two changes reinforce each other. The estimate exceeds the true difference by\n\\[E-(x-y)=2t>0.\\]\nHer estimate is necessarily larger than \\(x-y\\), choice A.",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
