"solution": "Let \\(e>0\\) be the common rounding amount. The rounded values are \\(x+e\\) and \\(y-e\\), so Xiaoli's estimate is\n\\[\n(x+e)-(y-e)=x-y+2e.\n\\]\nIncreasing the first number adds \\(e\\) to the difference, and decreasing the number being subtracted adds another \\(e\\). Her estimate therefore exceeds \\(x-y\\) by \\(2e>0\\). The answer is choice A.",
