"number": 19,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "A unit cube has vertices \\(P_1,\\) \\(P_2,\\) \\(P_3,\\) \\(P_4,\\) \\(P_1',\\) \\(P_2',\\) \\(P_3',\\) and \\(P_4'.\\) Vertices \\(P_2,\\) \\(P_3,\\) and \\(P_4\\) are adjacent to \\(P_1,\\) and for \\(1 \\le i \\le 4,\\) vertices \\(P_i\\) and \\(P_i'\\) are opposite to each other. A regular octahedron has one vertex in each of the segments \\(P_1P_2,\\) \\(P_1P_3,\\) \\(P_1P_4,\\) \\(P_1'P_2',\\) \\(P_1'P_3',\\) and \\(P_1'P_4'.\\) What is the octahedron’s side length?\n\n[Figure 1](figures/2012_AMC_12B_Q19_question_fig1.svg)",
"questionType": "mixed",
