"level": "AMC 10",
"batch": "A",
"number": 9,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "In a recent basketball game, Shenille attempted only three-point shots and two-point shots. She was successful on \\(20\\%\\) of her three-point shots and \\(30\\%\\) of her two-point shots. Shenille attempted \\(30\\) shots. How many points did she score?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(12\\)",
"B": "\\(18\\)",
"C": "\\(24\\)",
"D": "\\(30\\)",
"E": "\\(36\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "B",
"solution": "The useful observation is that the two success rates produce the same number of points per attempt within each shot category:\n\\[\n3\\cdot 20\\%=0.6,\n\\qquad\n2\\cdot 30\\%=0.6.\n\\]\nLet \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) be her numbers of three-point and two-point attempts. Then \\(x+y=30\\). Her successful shot counts are \\(0.20x\\) and \\(0.30y\\), so her actual score is\n\\[\n3(0.20x)+2(0.30y)\n=0.6(x+y)\n=0.6\\cdot30\n=18.\n\\]\nThus the unknown split between shot types does not affect the total. She scored \\(18\\) points, choice \\(\\mathrm{B}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
