"number": 22,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "The regular octagon \\(ABCDEFGH\\) has its center at \\(J.\\) Each of the vertices and the center are to be associated with one of the digits \\(1\\) through \\(9,\\) with each digit used once, in such a way that the sums of the numbers on the lines \\(AJE,\\) \\(BJF,\\) \\(CJG,\\) and \\(DJH\\) are all equal. In how many ways can this be done?\n\n[Figure 1](figures/2013_AMC_10B_Q22_question_fig1.svg)",
