"year": 2013,
"level": "AMC 12",
"batch": "A",
"number": 6,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "In a recent basketball game, Shenille attempted only three-point shots and two-point shots. She was successful on \\(20\\%\\) of her three-point shots and \\(30\\%\\) of her two-point shots. Shenille attempted \\(30\\) shots. How many points did she score?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(12\\)",
"B": "\\(18\\)",
"C": "\\(24\\)",
"D": "\\(30\\)",
"E": "\\(36\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "B",
"solution": "The useful observation is that the point value times the success rate is the same for both types of shot:\n\\[\n3\\cdot0.20=0.6,\n\\qquad\n2\\cdot0.30=0.6.\n\\]\nLet \\(u\\) and \\(v\\) be the numbers of three-point and two-point attempts, respectively. Every attempt belongs to exactly one group, so \\(u+v=30\\). She made \\(0.20u\\) three-point shots and \\(0.30v\\) two-point shots. Her total score was therefore\n\\[\n3(0.20u)+2(0.30v)\n=0.6(u+v)\n=0.6\\cdot30\n=18.\n\\]\nShe scored \\(18\\) points, choice B.",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
"sourceURL": "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/amc12/2013A/solutions",
