"number": 12,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "Cities \\(A,\\) \\(B,\\) \\(C,\\) \\(D,\\) and \\(E\\) are connected by roads \\(AB,\\) \\(AD,\\) \\(AE,\\) \\(BC,\\) \\(BD,\\) \\(CD,\\) and \\(DE.\\) How many different routes are there from \\(A\\) to \\(B\\) that use each road exactly once? (Such a route will necessarily visit some cities more than once.)\n\n[Figure 1](figures/2013_AMC_12B_Q12_question_fig1.svg)",
