"year": 2013,
"level": "AMC 8",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 9,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "The Incredible Hulk can double the distance he jumps with each succeeding jump. If his first jump is \\(1\\) meter, the second jump is \\(2\\) meters, the third jump is \\(4\\) meters, and so on, then on which jump will he first be able to jump more than \\(1\\) kilometer?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(9\\)th",
"B": "\\(10\\)th",
"C": "\\(11\\)th",
"D": "\\(12\\)th",
"E": "\\(13\\)th"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "C",
"solution": "One kilometer is \\(1000\\) meters, so we need the first jump whose distance exceeds \\(1000\\) meters. Starting with the first jump, repeatedly double the distance. The distances in meters are\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n&1,\\ 2,\\ 4,\\ 8,\\ 16,\\ 32,\\\\\n&64,\\ 128,\\ 256,\\ 512,\\ 1024.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nThese are the first through eleventh jumps, respectively. The tenth jump is \\(512\\) meters, and every earlier jump is shorter. The eleventh jump is \\(1024>1000\\) meters, so it is the first to exceed one kilometer. The answer is the \\(11\\)th jump, choice C.",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
