"year": 2013,
"level": "AMC 8",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 10,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "What is the ratio of the least common multiple of \\(180\\) and \\(594\\) to the greatest common factor of \\(180\\) and \\(594?\\)",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(110\\)",
"B": "\\(165\\)",
"C": "\\(330\\)",
"D": "\\(625\\)",
"E": "\\(660\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "C",
"solution": "Prime factorization shows which factors the two numbers share and which factors a common multiple must contain:\n\\[\n180=2^2\\cdot3^2\\cdot5,\n\\]\n\\[\n594=2\\cdot3^3\\cdot11.\n\\]\nA common factor can contain only primes appearing in both numbers, and cannot use more copies than either number contains. Taking as many shared copies as possible gives the greatest common factor:\n\\[\n2\\cdot3^2=18.\n\\]\nA common multiple must contain enough copies of every prime to be divisible by both numbers. Taking exactly the larger count of each prime gives the least common multiple:\n\\[\n2^2\\cdot3^3\\cdot5\\cdot11=5940.\n\\]\nThe requested ratio, with the least common multiple first, is\n\\[\n\\frac{5940}{18}=330.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(330\\), choice C.",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
"sourceURL": "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/amc8/2013/solutions",
