"level": "AMC 8",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 11,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "Ted’s grandfather used his treadmill on \\(3\\) days this week. He went \\(2\\) miles each day.\n\nOn Monday he jogged at a speed of \\(5\\) miles per hour. He walked at the rate of \\(3\\) miles per hour on Wednesday and at \\(4\\) miles per hour on Friday.\n\nIf Grandfather had always walked at \\(4\\) miles per hour, he would have spent less time on the treadmill. How many minutes less?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(1\\)",
"B": "\\(2\\)",
"C": "\\(3\\)",
"D": "\\(4\\)",
"E": "\\(5\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "D",
"solution": "An hour has \\(60\\) minutes. Dividing \\(60\\) by the speed in miles per hour gives the minutes needed for one mile. Each session covers \\(2\\) miles, so the session times in minutes are\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{Monday: }&2\\cdot(60\\div5)=24,\\\\\n\\text{Wednesday: }&2\\cdot(60\\div3)=40,\\\\\n\\text{Friday: }&2\\cdot(60\\div4)=30.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nHis actual total was \\(24+40+30=94\\) minutes.\n\nAt \\(4\\) miles per hour, every session would take \\(30\\) minutes, giving \\(3\\cdot30=90\\) minutes altogether. He would therefore spend \\(94-90=4\\) minutes less on the treadmill, choice D.",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
"sourceURL": "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/amc8/2013/solutions",
