"level": "AMC 8",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 12,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "At the \\(2013\\) Winnebago County Fair a vendor is offering a “fair special” on sandals. If you buy one pair of sandals at the regular price of \\(\\$50,\\) you get a second pair at a \\(40 \\%\\) discount, and a third pair at half the regular price.\n\nJavier took advantage of the “fair special” to buy three pairs of sandals. What percentage of the \\(\\$150\\) regular price did he save?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(25\\)",
"B": "\\(30\\)",
"C": "\\(33\\)",
"D": "\\(40\\)",
"E": "\\(45\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "B",
"solution": "A \\(40\\%\\) discount means paying \\(60\\%\\) of the regular price. Thus the second pair costs \\(50\\cdot0.60=30\\) dollars, and the third pair costs \\(50\\div2=25\\) dollars.\n\nJavier pays \\(50+30+25=105\\) dollars, saving \\(150-105=45\\) dollars. To find the percentage saved, compare this savings with the regular total:\n\\[\n\\frac{45}{150}=0.30=30\\%.\n\\]\nHe saved \\(30\\%\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{B}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
