"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "For real numbers \\( w \\) and \\( z ,\\) \\[ \\cfrac{\\frac{1}{w} + \\frac{1}{z}}{\\frac{1}{w} - \\frac{1}{z}} = 2014. \\] What is \\( \\frac{w+z}{w-z} ?\\)",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\( -2014 \\)",
"B": "\\( \\dfrac{-1}{2014} \\)",
"C": "\\( \\dfrac{1}{2014} \\)",
"D": "\\( 1 \\)",
"E": "\\( 2014 \\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "A",
"solution": "The reciprocals suggest multiplying both the numerator and denominator by \\(wz\\). The original expression is defined, so \\(w\\ne0\\), \\(z\\ne0\\), and \\(1/w-1/z\\ne0\\). The last condition also gives \\(w\\ne z\\).\n\nBecause \\(wz\\ne0\\), this multiplication preserves the fraction and gives\n\\[\n\\frac{\\frac1w+\\frac1z}{\\frac1w-\\frac1z}\n=\\frac{z+w}{z-w}=2014.\n\\]\nThe requested numerator is the same, while its denominator has the opposite sign: \\(w-z=-(z-w)\\). Therefore\n\\[\n\\frac{w+z}{w-z}\n=-\\frac{w+z}{z-w}\n=-2014.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice A.",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
