"batch": "A",
"number": 2,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "At the theater children get in for half price. The price for \\(5\\) adult tickets and \\(4\\) child tickets is \\(\\$24.50.\\) How much would \\(8\\) adult tickets and \\(6\\) child tickets cost?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(\\$35\\)",
"B": "\\(\\$38.50\\)",
"C": "\\(\\$40\\)",
"D": "\\(\\$42\\)",
"E": "\\(\\$42.50\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "B",
"solution": "Because a child ticket costs half as much as an adult ticket, four child tickets cost as much as \\(4\\cdot\\frac12=2\\) adult tickets. Thus the given purchase costs the same as \\(5+2=7\\) adult tickets, so one adult ticket costs\n\\[\n\\$24.50\\div7=\\$3.50.\n\\]\nSimilarly, six child tickets cost as much as three adult tickets. Therefore eight adult tickets and six child tickets cost\n\\[\n(8+3)(\\$3.50)=\\boxed{\\$38.50},\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\mathrm{B}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
