"number": 13,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "Real numbers \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) are chosen with \\(1 \\lt a \\lt b\\) such that no triangle with positive area has side lengths \\(1,\\) \\(a,\\) and \\(b\\) or \\(\\tfrac1b,\\) \\(\\tfrac1a,\\) and \\(1.\\) What is the smallest possible value of \\(b?\\)",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(\\dfrac{3+\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\)",
"B": "\\(\\dfrac{5}{2}\\)",
"C": "\\(\\dfrac{3+\\sqrt{5}}{2}\\)",
"D": "\\(\\dfrac{3+\\sqrt{6}}{2}\\)",
"E": "\\(3\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "C",
"solution": "For three positive lengths in increasing order, a triangle has positive area exactly when the two smaller lengths sum to more than the largest. Here \\(1<a<b\\), so the first proposed triangle fails exactly when\n\\[\n1+a\\le b,\n\\]\nor \\(a\\le b-1\\). In particular, \\(b>2\\).\n\nThe reciprocal lengths satisfy \\(1/b<1/a<1\\). Thus the second proposed triangle fails exactly when\n\\[\n\\frac1b+\\frac1a\\le1.\n\\]\nBecause \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(b-1\\) are positive, we may multiply and divide by them without changing the inequality direction. The reciprocal condition becomes\n\\[\na+b\\le ab,\n\\qquad a(b-1)\\ge b,\n\\qquad a\\ge\\frac{b}{b-1}.\n\\]\nThe lower and upper bounds on \\(a\\) must be compatible, so\n\\[\n\\frac{b}{b-1}\\le b-1\n\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\nb^2-3b+1\\ge0.\n\\]\nThe roots of \\(b^2-3b+1=0\\) are\n\\[\n\\frac{3-\\sqrt5}{2},\\qquad \\frac{3+\\sqrt5}{2}.\n\\]\nThe quadratic is nonnegative outside the interval between these roots. Since \\(b>2\\), only the upper range is possible:\n\\[\nb\\ge\\frac{3+\\sqrt5}{2}.\n\\]\nTo check attainment, take \\(a=(1+\\sqrt5)/2\\) and \\(b=a+1=(3+\\sqrt5)/2\\). These satisfy \\(1<a<b\\) and \\(a^2=a+1\\). Consequently,\n\\[\nab=a^2+a=2a+1=a+b,\n\\]\nso \\(1/a+1/b=1\\), while \\(1+a=b\\). Both triples are degenerate and therefore have no positive area, as required. The smallest possible value is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{3+\\sqrt5}{2}}\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{C}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
