"year": 2014,
"level": "AMC 8",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 21,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "The \\(7\\)-digit numbers \\(\\underline{74A52B1}\\) and \\(\\underline{326AB4C}\\) are each multiples of \\(3\\). Which of the following could be the value of \\(C\\)?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\( 1 \\)",
"B": "\\( 2 \\)",
"C": "\\( 3 \\)",
"D": "\\( 5 \\)",
"E": "\\( 8 \\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "A",
"solution": "A number is a multiple of \\(3\\) exactly when its digit sum is a multiple of \\(3\\). The two digit sums are\n\\[\n19+A+B\\quad\\text{and}\\quad15+A+B+C.\n\\]\nComparing them is useful because the shared digits \\(A\\) and \\(B\\) cancel. Since both sums are multiples of \\(3\\), their difference must also be a multiple of \\(3\\):\n\\[\n(15+A+B+C)-(19+A+B)=C-4.\n\\]\nBecause \\(C\\) is a digit from \\(0\\) through \\(9\\), this restricts \\(C\\) to \\(1,4,7\\). Only \\(1\\) appears among the choices.\n\nIt is attainable: choosing \\(A=0\\), \\(B=2\\), and \\(C=1\\) gives digit sums \\(21\\) and \\(18\\), both multiples of \\(3\\). Thus \\(C=1\\) could occur, choice A.",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
"sourceURL": "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/amc8/2014/solutions",
