"solution": "A negative integer exponent means taking the reciprocal of the corresponding positive power. Since \\(-2\\ne0\\),\n\\[\n(-2)^{-2}=\\frac{1}{(-2)^2}=\\frac14.\n\\]\nEvaluate this power before subtracting. The requested value is\n\\[\n2-\\frac14=\\frac84-\\frac14=\\boxed{\\frac74},\n\\]\nchoice C.",
