"year": 2015,
"level": "AMC 10",
"batch": "B",
"number": 7,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "Consider the operation “minus the reciprocal of,” defined by \\(a\\diamond b=a-\\frac{1}{b}.\\) What is \\[((1\\diamond2)\\diamond3)-(1\\diamond(2\\diamond3))?\\]",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\( -\\dfrac{7}{30} \\)",
"B": "\\( -\\dfrac{1}{6} \\)",
"C": "\\( 0 \\)",
"D": "\\( \\dfrac{1}{6} \\)",
"E": "\\( \\dfrac{7}{30} \\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "A",
"solution": "Evaluate the innermost operations first. The grouping matters because \\(a\\diamond b\\) subtracts the reciprocal of its second input.\n\nFor the first grouped expression,\n\\[\n(1\\diamond2)\\diamond3\n=\\left(1-\\frac12\\right)-\\frac13\n=\\frac16.\n\\]\nFor the second, first calculate\n\\[\n2\\diamond3=2-\\frac13=\\frac53.\n\\]\nIts reciprocal is \\(3/5\\), so\n\\[\n1\\diamond(2\\diamond3)=1-\\frac35=\\frac25.\n\\]\nThe second inputs used are \\(2\\), \\(3\\), and \\(5/3\\), all nonzero, so every operation is defined. The requested difference is\n\\[\n\\frac16-\\frac25=\\frac{5-12}{30}=\\boxed{-\\frac7{30}},\n\\]\nchoice A.",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
"sourceURL": "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/amc10/2015B/solutions",
