"level": "AMC 10",
"batch": "B",
"number": 10,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "What are the sign and units digit of the product of all the odd negative integers strictly greater than \\(-2015?\\)",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "It is a negative number ending with a \\(1.\\)",
"B": "It is a positive number ending with a \\(1.\\)",
"C": "It is a negative number ending with a\n\\(5.\\)",
"D": "It is a positive number ending with a \\(5.\\)",
"E": "It is a negative number ending with a \\(0.\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "C",
"solution": "We can find the sign and units digit without calculating the entire product. Since \\(-2015\\) is excluded, the factors are\n\\[\n-1,-3,-5,\\ldots,-2013.\n\\]\nThere are \\((2013+1)/2=1007\\) factors. An odd number of negative factors has a negative product.\n\nThe absolute value of the product contains a factor of \\(5\\), and all its factors are odd. It is therefore an odd multiple of \\(5\\). Multiples of \\(5\\) end in \\(0\\) or \\(5\\), and an odd number cannot end in \\(0\\). Thus the product is a negative number ending in \\(5\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{C}}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
