"batch": "NA",
"number": 8,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "What is the smallest whole number larger than the perimeter of any triangle with a side of length \\( 5\\) and a side of length \\(19?\\)",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\( 24 \\)",
"B": "\\( 29 \\)",
"C": "\\( 43 \\)",
"D": "\\( 48 \\)",
"E": "\\( 57 \\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "D",
"solution": "Let \\(x\\) be the third side length. The triangle inequalities give\n\\[\n19-5<x<19+5,\n\\]\nso \\(14<x<24\\). Both endpoints are excluded because equality would make the triangle flat.\n\nThe perimeter is therefore\n\\[\n5+19+x=24+x<48.\n\\]\nThus \\(48\\) is larger than every possible perimeter. To show it is the smallest such whole number, choose \\(x=23.5\\). This is an allowed third side because \\(14<23.5<24\\), and its perimeter is \\(47.5\\). Consequently, \\(47\\) and every smaller whole number fail to exceed every possible perimeter.\n\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{48}\\), choice \\(\\text{D}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
