"batch": "A",
"number": 7,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "The mean, median, and mode of the \\(7\\) data values \\[60, 100, x, 40, 50, 200, 90\\] are all equal to \\(x.\\) What is the value of \\(x?\\)",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(50\\)",
"B": "\\(60\\)",
"C": "\\(75\\)",
"D": "\\(90\\)",
"E": "\\(100\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "D",
"solution": "The mean condition gives an equation that determines \\(x\\). The six known values sum to\n\\[\n60+100+40+50+200+90=540.\n\\]\nSince the mean of all seven values is \\(x\\), their total must be \\(7x\\). Thus\n\\[\n540+x=7x,\n\\qquad 540=6x,\n\\qquad x=90.\n\\]\nWe must also check the median and mode. With \\(x=90\\), the values in increasing order are\n\\[\n40,50,60,90,90,100,200.\n\\]\nThe median is the fourth value, \\(90\\). The unique mode is also \\(90\\), because it occurs twice while every other value occurs once. Therefore \\(x=90\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
