"level": "AMC 10",
"batch": "B",
"number": 4,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "Zoey read \\(15\\) books, one at a time. The first book took her \\(1\\) day to read, the second book took her \\(2\\) days to read, the third book took her \\(3\\) days to read, and so on, with each book taking her \\(1\\) more day to read than the previous book. Zoey finished the first book on a Monday, and the second on a Wednesday. On what day of the week did she finish her \\(15\\)th book?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "Sunday",
"B": "Monday",
"C": "Wednesday",
"D": "Friday",
"E": "Saturday"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "B",
"solution": "Use the Monday when Zoey finished her first book as the starting point. That book is already finished, so the time until she finishes book \\(15\\) is\n\\[\n2+3+\\cdots+15.\n\\]\nPair the shortest remaining reading time with the longest. There are seven pairs, each totaling \\(17\\) days:\n\\[\n(2+15)+(3+14)+\\cdots+(8+9)\n=7\\cdot17=119.\n\\]\nSince \\(119=17\\cdot7\\), exactly \\(17\\) weeks pass. The weekday is therefore unchanged: she finishes on Monday, choice \\(\\mathrm{B}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Original Math Practice solution",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice",
