"number": 18,
"area": "Unclassified",
"question": "How many positive factors does \\(23{,}232\\) have?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\( 9 \\)",
"B": "\\( 12 \\)",
"C": "\\( 28 \\)",
"D": "\\( 36 \\)",
"E": "\\( 42 \\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "E",
"solution": "Prime factorization lets us construct every factor without listing them. First,\n\n\\[\n23{,}232=64\\cdot363=2^6\\cdot3\\cdot11^2.\n\\]\n\nAny positive factor must have the form \\(2^a3^b11^c\\), where \\(a\\) is from \\(0\\) to \\(6\\), \\(b\\) is \\(0\\) or \\(1\\), and \\(c\\) is \\(0,1,2\\). These choices give \\(7\\), \\(2\\), and \\(3\\) possibilities, respectively. Each combination gives a different factor, and every factor is obtained because no other prime is available.\n\nThe number of factors is \\(7\\cdot2\\cdot3=\\boxed{42}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{E}}\\). Include exponent zero for each prime, since a factor need not contain that prime.",
"solutionSource": "Adapted from MAA official solutions",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://drive.usercontent.google.com/uc?id=1RcfdsJkYkLvanhwRU9GWkLBt-2OlMOA0&export=download",
