"area": "Prealgebra",
"question": "Luka is making lemonade to sell at a school fundraiser. His recipe requires \\(4\\) times as much water as sugar and twice as much sugar as lemon juice. He uses \\(3\\) cups of lemon juice. How many cups of water does he need?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(6\\)",
"B": "\\(8\\)",
"C": "\\(12\\)",
"D": "\\(18\\)",
"E": "\\(24\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "E",
"solution": "Start with the ingredient amount we know and follow the recipe ratios. The sugar is twice the lemon juice, so \\(3\\) cups of lemon juice require \\(2\\cdot3=6\\) cups of sugar.\n\nThe water is four times the sugar, so Luka needs \\(4\\cdot6=\\boxed{24}\\) cups of water, choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{E}}\\). The two multipliers combine because they connect lemon juice to sugar and then sugar to water.",
