"year": 2020,
"level": "AMC 8",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 3,
"area": "Counting & Probability",
"question": "Carrie has a rectangular garden that measures \\(6\\) feet by \\(8\\) feet. She plants the entire garden with strawberry plants. Carrie is able to plant \\(4\\) strawberry plants per square foot, and she harvests an average of \\(10\\) strawberries per plant. How many strawberries can she expect to harvest?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(560\\)",
"B": "\\(960\\)",
"C": "\\(1120\\)",
"D": "\\(1920\\)",
"E": "\\(3840\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "D",
"solution": "First find how much planting space Carrie has. The garden's area is \\(6\\cdot8=48\\) square feet.\n\nAt \\(4\\) plants per square foot, that holds \\(48\\cdot4=192\\) plants. Each plant produces an average of \\(10\\) strawberries, so the expected harvest is\n\n\\[\n192\\cdot10=\\boxed{1920}\\text{ strawberries},\n\\]\n\nchoice \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\). The units guide the two steps: square feet to plants, then plants to strawberries.",
"solutionSource": "Adapted from MAA official solutions",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://drive.usercontent.google.com/uc?id=1pgLVYoFDn26DYpNrqfrtGWrh0JIpNOgE&export=download",
"sourceURL": "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/amc8/2020/solutions",
