"year": 2022,
"level": "AMC 8",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 6,
"area": "Algebra",
"question": "Three positive integers are equally spaced on a number line. The middle number is \\(15\\) and the largest number is \\(4\\) times the smallest number. What is the smallest of these three numbers?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(4\\)",
"B": "\\(5\\)",
"C": "\\(6\\)",
"D": "\\(7\\)",
"E": "\\(8\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "C",
"solution": "Equal spacing means the distance from the smallest number to \\(15\\) equals the distance from \\(15\\) to the largest number.\n\nLet the smallest number be \\(x\\). The largest is then \\(4x\\), so the two gaps give\n\n\\[\n15-x=4x-15.\n\\]\n\nAdding \\(x+15\\) to both sides gives \\(30=5x\\), hence \\(x=6\\).\n\nThe numbers \\(6,15,24\\) have equal gaps of \\(9\\), and \\(24=4\\cdot6\\). Thus the answer is \\(\\boxed{6}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{C}}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Adapted from MAA official solutions",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://drive.usercontent.google.com/uc?id=1h0XYnHhGAtM4i3JxvGUgozPrlhZiYZQb&export=download",
