"year": 2022,
"level": "AMC 8",
"batch": "NA",
"number": 8,
"area": "Counting & Probability",
"question": "What is the value of:\n\n\\[ \\dfrac{1}{3} \\cdot \\dfrac{2}{4} \\cdot \\dfrac{3}{5} \\cdots \\dfrac{18}{20} \\cdot \\dfrac{19}{21} \\cdot \\dfrac{20}{22} \\]",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(\\displaystyle \\dfrac{1}{462}\\)",
"B": "\\(\\displaystyle \\dfrac{1}{231}\\)",
"C": "\\(\\displaystyle \\dfrac{1}{132}\\)",
"D": "\\(\\displaystyle \\dfrac{2}{213}\\)",
"E": "\\(\\displaystyle \\dfrac{1}{22}\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "B",
"solution": "Write the product as one fraction so that its repeated factors are visible:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1\\cdot2\\cdot3\\cdots20}\n{3\\cdot4\\cdot5\\cdots22}.\n\\]\n\nEvery factor from \\(3\\) through \\(20\\) occurs once above and once below the fraction bar, so all of those factors cancel. What remains is\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1\\cdot2}{21\\cdot22}\n=\\frac{2}{462}\n=\\boxed{\\frac1{231}}.\n\\]\n\nThe answer is choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{B}}\\). In a product with shifted factors like this, look for the factors that survive at the two ends.",
"solutionSource": "Adapted from MAA official solutions",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://drive.usercontent.google.com/uc?id=1h0XYnHhGAtM4i3JxvGUgozPrlhZiYZQb&export=download",
