"number": 1,
"area": "Prealgebra",
"question": "What is the value of the following expression?\n\n\\[ (8 \\times 4 + 2) - (8 + 4 \\times 2) \\]",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(0\\)",
"B": "\\(6\\)",
"C": "\\(10\\)",
"D": "\\(18\\)",
"E": "\\(24\\)"
},
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "D",
"solution": "Multiplication comes before addition inside each pair of parentheses. Work out the two groups separately:\n\n\\[\n8\\times4+2=32+2=34,\n\\qquad\n8+4\\times2=8+8=16.\n\\]\n\nNow subtract the value of the second group from the first:\n\n\\[\n34-16=18.\n\\]\n\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{18}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\).",
"solutionSource": "Adapted from MAA official solutions",
"solutionSourceURL": "https://maa.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/2023_AMC8_Solutions_.pdf",
"sourceURL": "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/amc8/2023/solutions",
